'''George William Russell''' ({{IPAc-en|ɹ|ʌ|s|əl}}; born 15 February 1998) is a British [[racing driver]] who competes in [[Formula One]] for [[Mercedes-Benz in Formula One|Mercedes]]. Russell has won {{number to word|{{f1stat|RUS|wins}}}} [[Formula One Grands Prix]] across eight seasons.

Born and raised in [[King's Lynn]], Russell began competitive [[kart racing]] aged seven. After a successful karting career—culminating in back-to-back victories at the [[KF3|junior]] [[Karting European Championship|European Championship]] in 2011 and 2012—Russell graduated to [[junior formulae]]. He won his first title at the [[2014 BRDC Formula 4 Championship|2014 BRDC F4 Championship]]. He then won the [[2017 GP3 Series]] and the [[2018 FIA Formula 2 Championship]] back-to-back with [[ART Grand Prix|ART]], becoming the fifth driver to win the [[GP2 Series|GP2]]/[[FIA Formula 2 Championship|Formula 2]] championship in their rookie season and the second driver to win both titles in their respective rookie seasons.

A member of the [[Mercedes Junior Team]] since 2017, Russell signed for [[Williams Racing|Williams]] in {{F1|2019}} to partner [[Robert Kubica]], making his Formula One debut at the {{F1GP|2019|Australian}}. He substituted for [[Lewis Hamilton]] at the [[2020 Sakhir Grand Prix]] for [[Mercedes-Benz in Formula One|Mercedes]], but was denied victory due to a team error and a puncture after leading the majority of the race. Russell scored his maiden podium at the curtailed [[2021 Belgian Grand Prix]] with Williams. In {{F1|2022}}, Russell replaced [[Valtteri Bottas]] at Mercedes to partner Hamilton; in his first season, Russell achieved his maiden [[List of Formula One polesitters|pole position]] in [[2022 Hungarian Grand Prix|Hungary]] and his maiden [[List of Formula One Grand Prix winners|win]] in [[2022 São Paulo Grand Prix|São Paulo]], finishing fourth in the [[World Drivers' Championship]]. After a winless season for Mercedes in {{F1|2023}}, Russell won the [[2024 Austrian Grand Prix|Austrian]] and [[2024 Las Vegas Grand Prix|Las Vegas]] Grands Prix in {{F1|2024}}, followed by the [[2025 Canadian Grand Prix|Canadian]] and [[2025 Singapore Grand Prix|Singapore]] Grands Prix in {{F1|2025}}; in 2024, he also became the first driver in [[1994 Belgian Grand Prix|30 years]] to be disqualified from [[2024 Belgian Grand Prix|a race win]]. Amidst a new regulation cycle introduced for {{f1|2026}}, Mercedes emerged as the fastest team, with Russell winning the [[2026 Australian Grand Prix|Australian]] and [[2026 Austrian Grand Prix|Austrian]] Grands Prix.

As of the {{Latest F1GP}}, Russell has achieved {{f1stat|RUS|wins}} race wins, {{f1stat|RUS|poles}} pole positions, {{f1stat|RUS|fastestlaps}} fastest laps, and {{f1stat|RUS|podiums}} podiums in Formula One. Russell is contracted to remain at Mercedes until at least the end of the 2026 season.

==Early life==
Russell was born in [[King's Lynn]], [[Norfolk]],<ref name=":24">{{Cite web |last=Hudson |first=Molly |date=30 November 2024 |title=George Russell: I'm ready to fight Max Verstappen and take his title |url=https://www.thetimes.com/sport/formula-one/article/george-russell-im-ready-to-fight-against-max-and-win-the-title-bf0g22p3w |access-date=13 February 2025 |website=The Times |language=en}}</ref> to father Steve and mother Alison.<ref>{{Cite web|date=12 October 2018|title=Russell parents joy at Formula One deal|url=https://morningstaronline.co.uk/article/russell-parents-joy-formula-one-deal|access-date=30 July 2020|website=Morning Star|archive-date=12 October 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181012202452/https://morningstaronline.co.uk/article/russell-parents-joy-formula-one-deal|url-status=live}}</ref> His father managed a business selling seeds and [[pulses]],<ref name=":24" /> which he sold in 2012 to fund his son's junior racing career.<ref name=":53">{{Cite web |title=Farming News - Gleadell and Dunns announce merger |url=https://farming.co.uk/news/gleadell-and-dunns-announce-merger |access-date=12 February 2025 |website=farming.co.uk}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/formula-1/2022/11/19/george-russells-rise-f1-stardom-told-know-best/ |url-access=registration |title=George Russell's rise to F1 stardom – told by those that know him best |last=Cary |first=Tom |date=19 November 2022 |work=[[The Daily Telegraph]] |access-date=3 May 2025 |issn=0307-1235 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240521044534/https://www.telegraph.co.uk/formula-1/2022/11/19/george-russells-rise-f1-stardom-told-know-best/ |archive-date=21 May 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref> Russell is the youngest of three siblings, including sister Cara and brother Benjy.<ref name="auto">{{Cite web|title=F1: Beyond The Grid on Apple Podcasts|url=https://podcasts.apple.com/gb/podcast/f1-beyond-the-grid/id1405972616|access-date=30 July 2020|website=Apple Podcasts|archive-date=18 February 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210218081218/https://podcasts.apple.com/gb/podcast/f1-beyond-the-grid/id1405972616|url-status=live}}</ref> He grew up in [[Tydd St Giles]]/[[Wisbech]] and [[Castle Rising]].<ref name=":3">{{Cite web |title="Winning my first race was a lifelong dream of mine... |url=https://www.klmagazine.co.uk/articles/georgerussell |access-date=16 October 2024 |website=KL Magazine}}</ref>

Russell took up karting at the age of seven, following his brother Benjy, a competitive karter who won the 2007 [[Super 1 National Kart Championships|Super 1 National Kart Championship]] in the Rotax Max category.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Driver: Benjy Russell {{!}} Driver Database |url=https://www.driverdb.com/drivers/benjy-russell |access-date=16 October 2024 |website=www.driverdb.com}}</ref> Russell picked up his number 63 from the kart his brother rented at the time.<ref>{{cite web|last=Bart-Williams|first=Nadim|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.from-childhood-number-plates-to-karting-titles-why-each-driver-picked-their.49DqOwhvza1RRvE2Rgi1so.html|title=From childhood number plates to football heroes – Why each driver picked their F1 race number|website=formula1.com|date=8 February 2023|accessdate=8 February 2023|archive-date=8 February 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230208184047/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.from-childhood-number-plates-to-karting-titles-why-each-driver-picked-their.49DqOwhvza1RRvE2Rgi1so.html|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name=":3" /> Growing up, his father would intentionally overstate his lap times to motivate him to drive faster.<ref name=":47">{{Cite web |last=Russell |first=George |date=16 October 2025 |title=0.00 {{!}} By George Russell |url=https://www.theplayerstribune.com/george-russell-f1-racing-mercedes |access-date=21 October 2025 |website=The Players' Tribune |language=en-US}}</ref>

Russell attended [[Wisbech Grammar School]], but shifted to homeschooling so that he could devote more time to his racing career.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Wells |first=Jonathan |date=2020 |title=George Russell needs to get himself a hobby |url=https://www.thegentlemansjournal.com/article/george-russell-formula-one-racing-driver-interview-williams-mercedes/ |access-date=16 October 2024 |website=Gentleman's Journal}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |author=Chris Bishop |date=17 March 2019 |title=On eve of his first Grand Prix, Norfolk's F1 hope vows 'I want to be world champion' |url=https://www.edp24.co.uk/news/norfolk-george-russell-eyes-f1-world-title-1-5939919 |access-date=30 November 2019 |work=[[Eastern Daily Press]]}}</ref> At 18, he moved to [[Milton Keynes]] to be closer to his junior racing team.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Burnett |first=Tom |date=12 January 2021 |title=George Russell's F1 Williams to Mercedes move and his championship hopes |url=https://www.buckinghamshirelive.com/sport/formula-1/f1-george-russell-williams-mercedes-4878398 |access-date=16 October 2024 |website=Buckinghamshire Live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Alex Albon on his year on the sidelines, how Red Bull helped him get back on the grid, and the next chapter with Williams {{!}} Formula 1® |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/alex-albon-on-his-year-on-the-sidelines-how-red-bull-helped-him-get-back-on.52fTxzftrNFBlEJuk0wE1c |access-date=18 March 2025 |website=Formula 1® - The Official F1® Website |language=en}}</ref>

== Junior racing career ==
=== Karting (2006–2013) ===
Russell began [[karting]] in 2006 and progressed to the cadet class by 2009, becoming [[Motor Sports Association|MSA]] British champion and British Open champion. In 2010 he moved to the Rotax Mini Max category where he became Super One British champion, Formula Kart Stars British champion, and also won the Kartmasters British Grand Prix.

Russell graduated to the [[KF3]] class in 2011. He joined the Intrepid karting team with help from Intrepid's [[Alex Albon]];<ref name=":18">{{Cite web |last=Williams-Smith |first=Jake |date=13 January 2022 |title=George Russell: Turning down Toto Wolff and secret DTM test led me to Mercedes F1 drive |url=https://www.motorsportmagazine.com/articles/single-seaters/f1/george-russell-turning-down-toto-wolff-and-secret-dtm-test-led-me-to-mercedes-f1-drive/ |access-date=18 December 2024 |website=Motor Sport Magazine |language=en-GB}}</ref> his teammates that year included Albon and [[Charles Leclerc]].<ref name=":32" /> Russell became [[CIK-FIA Karting European Championship|CIK-FIA European Champion]] and won the [[SKUSA SuperNationals]] title, while Leclerc won the [[Karting World Cup]].<ref name=":32" /><ref name=":37">{{Cite web |last= |date=30 November 2012 |title=George Russell loses out on historic SKUSA title double |url=https://www.racecar.com/news/54018/motorsport/george-russell-loses-out-on-historic-skusa-title-double |access-date=5 March 2025 |website=Racecar |language=en}}</ref> In 2012, Russell became the first driver in history to successfully defend the [[Karting European Championship#Junior OK-Junior class (1989–present)|Junior European Championship]],<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.kartcom.com/en/news/2012/07/23/euro-kf3-russell-doubles-the-stakes/ |title=Euro KF3: Russell doubles the stakes |date=23 July 2012 |website=Kartcom |access-date=17 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241210021319/https://www.kartcom.com/en/news/2012/07/23/euro-kf3-russell-doubles-the-stakes/ |archive-date=10 December 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref> and nearly defended his SKUSA title following [[Lance Stroll]]'s disqualification, although Stroll's win was ultimately reinstated.<ref name=":37" /> In his final year of karting in 2013,<ref>{{cite news|url=http://www.formula4.com/drivers/2014-drivers/george-russell.aspx|title=Driver: George Russell|work=[[BRDC Formula 4 Championship]]|publisher=[[British Racing Drivers' Club]]|access-date=8 December 2014|archive-date=8 December 2014|archive-url=https://archive.today/20141208225452/http://www.formula4.com/drivers/2014-drivers/george-russell.aspx|url-status=dead}}</ref> Russell moved up to [[KF1]], finishing 19th in the [[Karting World Championship|CIK-FIA World Championship]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=2013 CIK-FIA World KF Championship Standings |url=https://www.fiakarting.com/championship-standings/2013-cik-fia-world-kf-championship-standings |access-date=5 March 2025 |website=FIA Karting}}</ref>

=== Formula 4 (2014) ===
In 2014, Russell made his [[Open wheel car|single-seater]] debut, simultaneously competing in [[2014 BRDC Formula 4 Championship season|BRDC Formula 4]] (Lanan Racing)<ref>{{cite news|url=http://www.formula4.com/news/multiple-karting-champion-george-russell-joins-f4-with-lanan-racing.aspx|title=Multiple Karting champion George Russell joins F4 with Lanan|work=[[BRDC Formula 4 Championship]]|publisher=[[British Racing Drivers' Club]]|date=6 December 2013|access-date=8 December 2014|archive-date=14 January 2014|archive-url=https://archive.today/20140114180318/http://www.formula4.com/news/multiple-karting-champion-george-russell-joins-f4-with-lanan-racing.aspx|url-status=dead}}</ref> and [[2014 Formula Renault 2.0 Alps season|Formula Renault 2.0 Alps]] ([[Koiranen GP]]).<ref name=":10">{{cite news |last=Allen |first=Peter |date=1 April 2014 |title=Russell and Tang set to move teams ahead of Alps opener |url=https://www.paddockscout.com/russell-and-tang-set-to-move-teams-ahead-of-alps-opener/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180829124638/http://www.paddockscout.com/russell-and-tang-set-to-move-teams-ahead-of-alps-opener |archive-date=29 August 2018 |access-date=8 December 2014 |work=paddockscout.com |publisher=Paddock Scout}}</ref> He led most of the BRDC F4 season, but lost the points lead to teammate [[Arjun Maini]] before the final race at [[Snetterton Motor Racing Circuit|Snetterton]],<ref>{{Cite web |last=Allen |first=Peter |date=17 December 2014 |title=PaddockScout Top 50 Drivers of 2014: 30-21 |url=https://formulascout.com/paddockscout-top-50-drivers-of-2014-30-21/23276 |access-date=18 December 2024 |website=Formula Scout |language=en-US}}</ref> which ''Formula Scout'' attributed to a mid-season case of [[chickenpox]].<ref name=":32">{{Cite web |last=Allen |first=Peter |date=27 June 2020 |title=When Leclerc, Russell and Albon stood out in F3 |url=https://formulascout.com/when-leclerc-russell-and-albon-stood-out-in-f3/63527 |access-date=5 March 2025 |website=Formula Scout |language=en-US}}</ref> He won that race to claim the title.<ref>{{cite news |date=26 October 2014 |title=Race Three Title Permutations |url=http://www.formula4.com/news/race-three-title-permutations.aspx |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://archive.today/20141208225441/http://www.formula4.com/news/race-three-title-permutations.aspx |archive-date=8 December 2014 |access-date=8 December 2014 |work=[[BRDC Formula 4 Championship]] |publisher=[[British Racing Drivers' Club]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last=Allen |first=Peter |date=26 October 2014 |title=George Russell wins BRDC F4 title decider to steal crown |url=https://www.paddockscout.com/george-russell-wins-brdc-f4-title-decider-to-steal-crown/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181125204203/http://www.paddockscout.com/george-russell-wins-brdc-f4-title-decider-to-steal-crown |archive-date=25 November 2018 |access-date=8 December 2014 |work=paddockscout.com |publisher=Paddock Scout}}</ref> As a reward, he was granted a GP3 test at [[Yas Marina Circuit|Yas Marina]].<ref>{{cite news |last=Allen |first=Peter |date=27 November 2014 |title=Ceccon leads Jones and Russell as GP3 test begins |url=https://www.paddockscout.com/ceccon-leads-jones-and-russell-as-gp3-test-begins/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181201005122/http://www.paddockscout.com/ceccon-leads-jones-and-russell-as-gp3-test-begins |archive-date=1 December 2018 |access-date=8 December 2014 |work=paddockscout.com |publisher=Paddock Scout}}</ref>

=== Formula Renault 2.0 (2014) ===
Russell had a more difficult season in Formula Renault 2.0 Alps. Although he was initially supposed to race for [[Prema Powerteam|Prema]], [[Lance Stroll]]'s father (Prema's part-owner and main funder) vetoed Russell from the team,<ref name=":11">{{Cite web |last=Mitchell-Malm |first=Scott |date=15 November 2022 |title=Two weeks in 2014 that made Russell's entire career |url=https://www.the-race.com/formula-1/two-weeks-in-2014-that-made-russells-entire-career/ |access-date=25 November 2024 |website=The Race}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Simmons |first=Marcus |date=23 June 2020 |title=George Russell's top 10 drives ranked |url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/george-russells-top-10-drives-ranked-4981730/4981730/ |access-date=25 November 2024 |work=Autosport}}</ref> even though Stroll was racing in [[2014 Italian F4 Championship|Italian F4]] and not Formula Renault. Russell found a landing spot with Koiranen,<ref name=":10" /> which dominated the season, scoring 423 points to Prema's 61. However, Russell was outshone by his Koiranen teammate [[Nyck de Vries]] (three years his elder), who won nine out of twelve races.<ref>{{cite news |title=Formula Renault 2.0 Alps 2014 standings |url=https://www.driverdb.com/championships/standings/formula-renault-20-alps/2014/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210510191528/https://www.driverdb.com/championships/standings/formula-renault-20-alps/2014/ |archive-date=10 May 2021 |access-date=8 December 2014 |work=driverdb.com |publisher=Driver Database}}</ref> Looking back, Russell said that [[Tech 1 Racing]] (his other option to replace Prema) would have been a better fit,<ref name=":11" /> but strongly praised de Vries, remarking that he "was always one of the very best,"<ref>{{Cite news |last=Coleman |first=Madeline |title=Nyck de Vries' long road to an F1 driver's seat — and his own definition of success |url=https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/4628486/2023/06/22/nyck-de-vries-f1-alpha-tauri/ |access-date=25 November 2024 |work=The New York Times |issn=0362-4331}}</ref> and that especially "in go-karting, he was the man to beat."<ref>{{Cite news |last=Cooper |first=Adam |date=16 October 2022 |title=Russell: De Vries Deserved to Have 'Stars Align' for F1 Entry |url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/russell-de-vries-deserved-to-have-stars-align-for-f1-entry/10385197/ |access-date=5 March 2025 |work=[[Motorsport.com]]}}</ref>

Russell's season ended on a high note after talent scout Gwen Lagrue (who later recruited him to Mercedes) arranged for him to join Tech 1 for the final round of the [[2014 Eurocup Formula Renault 2.0 season|Eurocup Formula Renault 2.0 season]] at [[Circuito de Jerez|Jerez]].<ref name=":48">{{Cite news |last=Smith |first=Luke |date=27 June 2023 |title=The F1 talent guru scouting, recruiting, and nurturing Mercedes' young drivers |url=https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/4641182/2023/06/27/f1-mercedes-gwen-lagrue-talent-scout/ |access-date=21 October 2025 |work=The New York Times |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331}}</ref> Eurocup was a higher level of competition than Alps.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Allen |first=Peter |date=6 January 2016 |title=Formula Renault 2.0 Alps won't run in 2016 |url=https://formulascout.com/formula-renault-2-0-alps-cancelled-for-2016/32829 |access-date=22 October 2025 |website=Formula Scout |language=en-US}}</ref><ref name=":11" /> Nonetheless, Russell won the final race of the Eurocup season, holding off a hard-charging de Vries and finishing 23.057 seconds ahead of his Tech 1 teammate [[Anthoine Hubert]].<ref>{{cite news |last=Khorounzhiy |first=Valentin |date=19 October 2014 |title=Guest driver George Russell delivers Tech 1's first Eurocup win of 2014 |url=https://www.paddockscout.com/guest-driver-george-russell-delivers-tech-1s-first-eurocup-win-of-2014/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181013053827/http://www.paddockscout.com/guest-driver-george-russell-delivers-tech-1s-first-eurocup-win-of-2014 |archive-date=13 October 2018 |access-date=8 December 2014 |work=paddockscout.com |publisher=Paddock Scout}}</ref>

At the end of the season, Russell won the [[Autosport BRDC Award]] after successfully testing [[Formula Two]], [[Deutsche Tourenwagen Masters|DTM]], and GT3 cars.<ref name=":12">{{cite news |last=Mitchell |first=Scott |date=7 December 2014 |title=George Russell wins 2014 McLaren AUTOSPORT BRDC Award |url=http://www.autosport.com/news/report.php/id/117079 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160303212734/http://www.autosport.com/news/report.php/id/117079 |archive-date=3 March 2016 |access-date=8 December 2014 |work=[[Autosport]] |publisher=[[Haymarket Media Group|Haymarket Publications]]}}</ref> At seventeen, he was the youngest-ever winner of the award; the BRDC lowered the entry age to accommodate him.<ref name=":11" /><ref name=":12" /> He was also selected for the BRDC's SuperStars junior driver mentorship programme, where he was once again the youngest-ever selection.<ref>{{cite news |date=23 February 2015 |title=BRDC announces 2015 SuperStars |url=http://www.brdc.co.uk/BRDC-Announces-2015-SuperStars |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181016165115/http://www.brdc.co.uk/BRDC-Announces-2015-SuperStars |archive-date=16 October 2018 |access-date=8 April 2015 |work=brdc.co.uk |publisher=[[British Racing Drivers' Club]] |quote=I am particularly delighted to announce five new SuperStars this year and welcome our youngest ever recruit George Russell to the programme...}}</ref>

=== Formula Three (2015–2016) ===
==== 2015: Debut in FIA European F3 and Masters podium ====
[[File:George Russell, Formel 3 2015 (cropped).JPG|thumb|left|Russell competing at [[Circuit de Spa-Francorchamps|Spa]] during the [[2015 FIA Formula 3 European Championship]]]]
Although Russell was expected to spend 2015 competing full-time in Eurocup Formula Renault 2.0, his BRDC Award win prompted him to skip directly to European [[Formula Three]],<ref>{{Cite web |last=Allen |first=Peter |date=9 April 2015 |title=2015 FIA F3 European Championship driver-by-driver preview |url=https://formulascout.com/2015-fia-f3-european-championship-driver-by-driver-preview/26041 |access-date=18 December 2024 |website=Formula Scout |language=en-US}}</ref> where he spent the next two years.

In 2015, Russell drove for [[Carlin Motorsport|Carlin]], a [[Volkswagen]] affiliate.<ref>{{cite news|title=McLaren AUTOSPORT BRDC Award winner Russell seals European F3 deal|url=http://www.autosport.com/news/report.php/id/117324|first=Marcus|last=Simmons|work=[[Autosport]]|publisher=[[Haymarket Media Group|Haymarket Publications]]|date=9 January 2015|access-date=9 January 2015|archive-date=3 March 2016|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160303213317/http://www.autosport.com/news/report.php/id/117324|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name=":18" /> He finished sixth,<ref>{{cite news |title=FIA Formula 3 European Championship 2015 standings |work=driverdb.com |publisher=Driver Database |url=https://www.driverdb.com/championships/standings/formula-3-europe/2015/ |access-date=18 November 2015 |archive-date=5 July 2015 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150705080438/https://www.driverdb.com/championships/standings/formula-3-europe/2015/ |url-status=live}}</ref> winning one race<ref>{{cite news|title=George Russell claims victory in second Formula 3 start|url=http://www.paddockscout.com/george-russell-claims-victory-in-second-formula-3-start/26323|first=Peter|last=Allen|work=paddockscout.com|publisher=Paddock Scout|date=11 April 2015|access-date=11 April 2015|archive-date=27 November 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181127152001/http://www.paddockscout.com/george-russell-claims-victory-in-second-formula-3-start/26323|url-status=live}}</ref> and collecting three podiums; ''PaddockScout'' opined that his qualifying pace was "his one obvious weak-spot,"<ref>{{Cite web |last=Allen |first=Peter |date=17 November 2015 |title=2015 FIA F3 European Championship season review |url=https://formulascout.com/2015-fia-f3-european-championship-season-review/31898 |access-date=18 December 2024 |website=Formula Scout |language=en-US}}</ref> and that he primarily stood out for his race pace and ability to cleanly overtake other drivers.<ref name=":32" /> He was second in the Rookies' Championship, behind Charles Leclerc,<ref>{{cite news|title=Rookie George Russell's debut in a Formula 1 car |url=http://www.fiaf3europe.com/en/news/Rookie-George-Russells-debut-in-a-Formula-1-car.html |work=fiaf3europe.com |publisher=[[European Formula 3 Championship]] |date=23 October 2015 |access-date=18 November 2015 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20151119063603/http://www.fiaf3europe.com/en/news/Rookie-George-Russells-debut-in-a-Formula-1-car.html |archive-date=19 November 2015 }}</ref> although fellow rookie [[Lance Stroll]] finished above him in the overall classification (the Rookies' Championship re-scores each race to remove non-rookies). He also finished second at the [[2015 Masters of Formula 3]] exhibition race, behind [[Antonio Giovinazzi]].<ref>{{cite news |title=Giovinazzi seals Masters of F3 title with dominant victory |url=http://www.paddockscout.com/giovinazzi-seals-masters-of-f3-title-with-dominant-victory/30852 |first=Gruz |last=David |work=paddockscout.com |publisher=Paddock Scout |date=20 September 2015 |access-date=18 November 2015 |archive-date=30 November 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181130202207/http://www.paddockscout.com/giovinazzi-seals-masters-of-f3-title-with-dominant-victory/30852 |url-status=live}}</ref>

==== 2016: Third in Europe with Hitech ====
In [[2016 FIA Formula 3 European Championship|2016]], Russell switched to [[Hitech GP]], a new Mercedes affiliate which was competing in its first full European Formula Three season.<ref name=":18" /> That year, Prema allegedly received special engines from Mercedes<ref>{{Cite web |last=Chachra |first=Tanish |date=16 April 2023 |title='It's Not a Fair Fight': George Russell Once Got Irked With Mercedes Helping Lance Stroll |url=https://thesportsrush.com/f1-news-its-not-a-fair-fight-george-russell-once-got-irked-with-mercedes-helping-lance-stroll/ |access-date=25 November 2024 |website=The Sports Rush}}</ref> and technical support (including a suspension upgrade) from [[Williams Racing|Williams]].<ref>{{Cite news |last=Simmons |first=Marcus |date=16 July 2016 |title=Prema plays down Williams F1 team's involvement in F3 project |url=https://www.autosport.com/fia-f3/news/prema-plays-down-williams-f1-teams-involvement-in-f3-project-5040668/5040668/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241201194329/https://www.autosport.com/fia-f3/news/prema-plays-down-williams-f1-teams-involvement-in-f3-project-5040668/5040668/ |archive-date=1 December 2024 |access-date=23 December 2024 |language=en |url-status=live }}</ref> Stroll (whose family was funding Prema<ref name=":42">{{Cite web |date=4 November 2016 |title=Report: Lance Stroll's father spent $80 million to get son Williams F1 seat |url=https://www.autoweek.com/racing/formula-1/a1857276/report-lance-strolls-father-spent-80-million-get-son-f1-seat/ |access-date=20 September 2024 |website=Autoweek}}</ref>) cruised to the title, with Russell finishing third, behind Prema drivers Stroll and [[Maximilian Günther]].<ref name=":19">{{Cite web |last=Allen |first=Peter |date=28 November 2018 |title=How George Russell developed to become Williams' ideal driver |url=https://formulascout.com/how-george-russell-developed-to-become-williams-ideal-driver/46493 |access-date=20 December 2024 |website=Formula Scout |language=en-US}}</ref> Nonetheless, Mercedes was impressed by Russell's performances and signed him to its driver academy at the end of the season.<ref name=":8">{{Cite news |last=Mitchell |first=Scott |date=28 August 2019 |title=The F1 lessons George Russell took from 'almost laughable' F3 year |url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/the-f1-lessons-george-russell-took-from-almost-laughable-f3-year-4989545/4989545/ |access-date=25 November 2024 |work=Autosport}}</ref> After making it to Formula One, Russell questioned the fairness of the 2016 competition, stating that it was "almost laughable to see ... how wrong that championship was."<ref name=":8" />

=== Mercedes Junior Team ===
{{Quote box
| quote = I had other F1 teams speak to me before Mercedes ... and it felt like they didn't even care. Because in this time, junior programs were not a thing. I think McLaren had one driver, Mercedes had one driver, Ferrari had ... maybe [[Jules Bianchi]], but he was already in Formula One. And Red Bull had, of course, maybe five or six. ... So, I just thought, you know, "I need to do something that ... will be memorable."
| author = Russell recalling his Mercedes PowerPoint presentation<ref>{{Cite AV media |url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=d53jwQHc4Yg |title=Taylor Swift concerts, Kimi's maths homework and George's PowerPoint {{!}} TeamMates Ep 3 |date=8 May 2025 |last=Mercedes-AMG Petronas Formula One Team |access-date=8 May 2025 |via=YouTube}}</ref>
| align = right
| width = 300px
}}
As Russell advanced through the junior pyramid, the costs of racing grew significantly. He estimated that it cost "£50K a year if you want to compete, £200K if you want to win."<ref name=":45">{{Cite web |last=White |first=Sam |date=21 March 2022 |title=Can anyone stop George Russell? Formula 1's wonderkid won't settle for second best |url=https://www.gq-magazine.co.uk/sport/article/george-russell-interview |access-date=4 October 2024 |website=British GQ}}</ref> Steve Russell spent roughly £1.5m to fund his son's junior career.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Meade |first=Samuel |date=4 May 2025 |title=George Russell's dad paid £1.5m to fund his career - but there was a catch |url=https://www.edinburghlive.co.uk/news/uk-world-news/george-russells-dad-paid-15m-31570543 |access-date=8 May 2025 |website=Edinburgh Live |language=en}}</ref> When Russell was sixteen, his father explained that he could not keep on funding him and that Russell needed to find a junior driver programme.<ref name=":45" /><ref name=":47" /> (Not long after that, Russell faced an £800K bill for a single Formula Two season.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Benson |first=Andrew |date=2026-04-16 |title=F1: Do you have to be a millionaire to make it to the top of the sport? |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/formula1/articles/c5y77exrqkeo |access-date=2026-04-16 |website=BBC Sport |language=en-GB}}</ref>)

Russell applied for a spot on the [[Mercedes Junior Team]]. Unlike modern Formula One driver academies, [[Mercedes-Benz in Formula One|Mercedes]] signed only one driver at a time, although it funded additional drivers on a short-term basis.<ref name=":47" /> To sway Mercedes leadership, Russell prepared a [[Microsoft PowerPoint]] presentation explaining why the team should sign him.<ref>{{cite web |date=19 January 2017 |title=British racing driver George Russell added to Mercedes' junior programme |url=http://www.espn.co.uk/f1/story/_/id/18508537/british-racing-driver-george-russell-added-mercedes-junior-programme |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170202000504/http://www.espn.co.uk/f1/story/_/id/18508537/british-racing-driver-george-russell-added-mercedes-junior-programme |archive-date=2 February 2017 |access-date=19 January 2017 |website=ESPN}}</ref>

To audition Russell for a full-time academy spot, Mercedes boss [[Toto Wolff]] offered to fund Russell's 2015 European Formula Three season. However, Mercedes's top F3 affiliate was Prema, from which Russell had already been vetoed. Russell chose [[Volkswagen]], which did not have a Formula One team at the time.<ref name=":18" /> At season's end, [[BMW]] offered him a [[Deutsche Tourenwagen Masters|DTM]] drive, but Mercedes persuaded him to bet on himself, offering him funding for a second F3 season<ref name=":18" /><ref name=":48" /> and making him the senior team's simulator driver.<ref>{{cite web |last=Velasco |first=Paul |date=12 March 2022 |title=Russell: In 2016 I was quite sure my F1 dream was over |url=https://www.grandprix247.com/2022/03/12/russell-in-2016-i-was-quite-sure-my-f1-dream-was-over/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221114201151/https://www.grandprix247.com/2022/03/12/russell-in-2016-i-was-quite-sure-my-f1-dream-was-over/ |archive-date=14 November 2022 |accessdate=14 November 2022 |website=grandprix247.com}}</ref> Russell switched to a Mercedes-powered F3 team for 2016.<ref name=":18" />

In early 2017, Russell officially joined the Mercedes Junior Team.<ref>{{cite news |date=19 January 2017 |title=George Russell: World champions Mercedes sign teenager from King's Lynn |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/38679732 |access-date=19 January 2021 |work=BBC Sport}}</ref> Wolff "set hard targets" for Russell, asking him to win the GP3 and Formula 2 titles before progressing to Formula One.<ref>{{Cite web |date=14 December 2022 |title='We've always set hard targets' – Wolff on Russell's rise from PowerPoint presentation to Grand Prix winner {{!}} Formula 1® |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/weve-always-set-hard-targets-wolff-on-russells-rise-from-powerpoint.6wTzk7i9jneeTTrovaqVs7 |access-date=4 October 2024 |website=Formula 1® - The Official F1® Website}}</ref>

=== GP3 Series (2017) ===
[[File:George Russell on 26 August 2017 at Spa-Francorchamps.jpg|alt=George Russell GP3 Series during Spa GP 2017|thumb|Russell racing at the 2017 Spa-Francorchamps GP3 round]]
With financial help from Mercedes, Russell secured a drive with [[ART Grand Prix]] for the [[2017 GP3 Series|2017 season]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.gp3series.com/News/2017/01_January/George-Russell-to-race-with-ART-Grand-Prix-in-2017/|title=George Russell to race with ART Grand Prix in 2017|date=19 January 2017|access-date=19 January 2017|archive-date=23 February 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180223214626/http://www.gp3series.com/News/2017/01_January/George-Russell-to-race-with-ART-Grand-Prix-in-2017/|url-status=live}}</ref>  ART was GP3's dominant team, having won six of the last seven team titles. In 2017, it swept the top four places in the standings.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Hewitt |first=Chloe |date=11 December 2017 |title=Season Review: 2017 GP3 Series - Russell Reigns Supreme |url=https://www.thecheckeredflag.co.uk/2017/12/season-review-2017-gp3-series-russell-reigns-supreme/ |access-date=5 March 2025 |website=The Checkered Flag |language=en-GB}}</ref>

Russell won the title as a rookie,<ref name=":9">{{Cite web |last=Larkam |first=Lewis |date=8 October 2017 |title=Mercedes junior Russell takes GP3 title |url=https://www.espn.com/f1/story/_/id/20953371/mercedes-junior-george-russell-takes-gp3-title |access-date=5 March 2025 |website=ESPN |language=en}}</ref> scoring four wins and finishing 79 points ahead of the second-placed [[Jack Aitken]].<ref>{{Cite news |last=Khorounzhiy |first=Valentin |date=18 January 2018 |title=Mercedes F1 protege and GP3 champion Russell gets 2018 ART F2 seat |url=https://www.autosport.com/formula2/news/mercedes-f1-protege-and-gp3-champion-russell-gets-2018-art-f2-seat-4987293/4987293/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241219093155/https://www.autosport.com/formula2/news/mercedes-f1-protege-and-gp3-champion-russell-gets-2018-art-f2-seat-4987293/4987293/ |archive-date=19 December 2024 |access-date=5 March 2025 |work=Autosport |language=en |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Francis |first=Anna |date=11 November 2024 |title=IN NUMBERS: How Kick Sauber signing Gabriel Bortoleto's F2 and F3 career compares to Leclerc, Russell and Piastri {{!}} Formula 1® |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/in-numbers-how-kick-sauber-signing-bortoletos-f2-and-f3-career-compares-to.2mA0DFlYBjsD1I9XFmfMok |access-date=5 March 2025 |website=Formula 1® - The Official F1® Website |language=en}}</ref> He locked up the title with two races to go.<ref name=":9" /> Notable races included a dominant performance at [[Circuit de Spa-Francorchamps|Spa-Francorchamps]] (a win, a second place, two poles, and two fastest laps)<ref>{{Cite news|url=https://www.autosport.com/gp3/news/131445/russell-takes-third-win-leading-an-art-123|title=Spa GP3: Mercedes junior George Russell leads ART 1–2–3 to victory|last=Kalinaukas|first=Alex|work=Autosport.com|access-date=14 October 2017|archive-date=28 September 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180928161253/https://www.autosport.com/gp3/news/131445/russell-takes-third-win-leading-an-art-123|url-status=live}}</ref> and a close three-way battle at [[Monza Circuit|Monza]].<ref>{{Cite news|url=https://www.autosport.com/gp3/news/131614/russell-wins-monza-gp3-thriller|title=Mercedes F1's George Russell wins thrilling Monza GP3 race|last=Kalinauckas|first=Alex|work=Autosport.com|access-date=14 October 2017|archive-date=31 August 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180831002452/https://www.autosport.com/gp3/news/131614/russell-wins-monza-gp3-thriller|url-status=live}}</ref>
=== FIA Formula 2 (2018) ===
[[File:FIA F2 Austria 2018 podium national anthems.jpg|left|thumb|Russell on the podium alongside [[Lando Norris]] (left) and [[Antonio Fuoco]] (right) after winning the [[2018 Spielberg Formula 2 round]]]]
[[File:George Russell, ART Grand Prix F2 Team (42837176685).jpg|thumb|Russell at the [[2018 Silverstone Formula 2 round]]]]
ART promoted Russell to its Formula Two team for the [[2018 Formula 2 Championship|2018 season]].<ref>{{Cite news |last=Khorounzhiy |first=Valentin |date=18 January 2018 |title=Mercedes F1 protege and GP3 champion Russell gets 2018 ART F2 seat |url=https://www.autosport.com/formula2/news/mercedes-f1-protege-and-gp3-champion-russell-gets-2018-art-f2-seat-4987293/4987293/ |access-date=26 November 2024 |work=Autosport}}</ref> In addition, Mercedes promoted Russell to first-team reserve driver, sharing duties with [[Pascal Wehrlein]].<ref>{{Cite news |last=Mitchell |first=Scott |title=Wehrlein, Russell to share Mercedes F1 reserve driver role in 2018 |url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/134490/wehrlein-russell-to-share-mercedes-reserve-role |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180223171351/https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/134490/wehrlein-russell-to-share-mercedes-reserve-role |archive-date=23 February 2018 |access-date=27 June 2018 |work=Autosport.com}}</ref> The 2018 F2 grid was "possibly the strongest field of the last decade",<ref>{{Cite web |last=Allen |first=Peter |date=26 November 2023 |title=Every GP2/F2 champion ranked |url=https://www.the-race.com/formula-1/every-gp2-f2-champion-ranked/ |access-date=26 November 2024 |website=The Race}}</ref> and featured several future F1 racers, including [[Lando Norris]], Alex Albon, [[Nyck de Vries]], and [[Nicholas Latifi]].<ref name=":34">{{Cite web |title=Driver Standings for the FIA Formula 2 2018 Championship |url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Standings/Driver?seasonId=175 |access-date=5 March 2025 |website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website |language=en}}</ref>

ART did not carry over its lopsided dominance from the prior year's F3 season, as Norris's Carlin took the teams' championship.<ref>{{Cite web |title=2018 FIA F2 Standings and Results in Motorsport |url=https://www.autosport.com/formula2/standings/2018/ |access-date=5 March 2025 |website=Autosport}}</ref> Although Formula Two is a [[spec series]] and every engine is built by the same company,<ref>{{Cite news |last=Smith |first=Luke |title=How Formula 2 became the launchpad for F1's next generation |url=https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/4610017/2023/06/15/formula-2-formula-1-drivers-development-differences/ |access-date=5 March 2025 |work=The New York Times |date=23 July 2023 |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331}}</ref> Russell, Albon, and Norris agreed that in practice, teams had engines of varying quality. Albon and Norris said that Russell had the best engine that year, while Russell and Albon said that Norris's engine was very competitive early in the season.<ref>{{Cite AV media |url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=89-GJHoqtiQ |title=Rookies Reunited {{!}} Catching Up With George, Lando and Alex! |date=30 September 2023 |last=((FORMULA 1)) |access-date=5 March 2025 |via=YouTube}} (0:35-1:12)</ref> After ten races, Norris led the standings.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Wood |first=Ida |date=30 December 2019 |title=Formula Scout Review of the 2010s Part 2: 2015 - 2019 |url=https://formulascout.com/formula-scout-review-of-the-2010s-part-2-2015-2019/58148 |access-date=5 March 2025 |website=Formula Scout |language=en-US}}</ref> Russell heated up at midseason, finishing either first or second in five out of six races. He qualified in the top four at all but one race (where he had engine trouble).<ref name=":35" /> He won the title, finishing 68 points ahead of the second-placed Norris.<ref name=":35">{{Cite web |last=Suttill |first=Josh |date=23 December 2018 |title=The top 10 Formula 2 drivers of 2018 |url=https://formulascout.com/the-top-10-formula-2-drivers-of-2018/46878 |access-date=5 March 2025 |website=Formula Scout |language=en-US}}</ref><ref name=":34" />

With his title, Russell became the fifth rookie champion of the GP2/F2 category (previously achieved by [[Nico Rosberg]], [[Lewis Hamilton]], [[Nico Hülkenberg]], and [[Charles Leclerc]]), the fourth driver to win the GP3/F3 and GP2/F2 titles in consecutive seasons (after Hamilton, Hülkenberg and Leclerc), and the second driver to win both of these titles as a rookie (after Leclerc). [[Oscar Piastri]] and [[Gabriel Bortoleto]] subsequently matched each of these feats.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Thoughts of a Champion – Gabriel Bortoleto |url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/5nmZgnPCjeSEnjCUPKS99d/thoughts-of-a-champion-gabriel-bortoleto |access-date=9 December 2024 |website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website}}</ref>
{{clear}}
==Formula One career==
In October 2015, Russell drove a Formula One car for the first time, when he tested the [[McLaren MP4-26]] at [[Silverstone Circuit|Silverstone]] as a prize for winning the 2014 [[Autosport BRDC Award]].<ref>{{cite web |last=Turner |first=Kevin |date=22 October 2015 |title=McLaren Autosport BRDC Award winner Russell completes prize F1 test |url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/mclaren-autosport-brdc-award-winner-russell-completes-prize-f1-test-4998645/4998645/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221114201150/https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/mclaren-autosport-brdc-award-winner-russell-completes-prize-f1-test-4998645/4998645/ |archive-date=14 November 2022 |accessdate=14 November 2022 |website=autosport.com}}</ref> After he joined the [[Mercedes Junior Team]], Mercedes gave him more testing opportunities. He drove a Mercedes for the first time in April 2017, testing the 2015 [[Mercedes F1 W06 Hybrid|Mercedes W06]] at [[Portimão Circuit|Portimão]].<ref name=":36">{{Cite web |last= |first= |date=24 June 2017 |title=Mercedes-AMG Petronas Motorsport – George Russell to test W08 in Budapest |url=https://www.mercedesamgf1.com/en/mercedes-amg-f1/george-russell-to-test-w08-in-budapest/ |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190523211052/https://www.mercedesamgf1.com/en/mercedes-amg-f1/george-russell-to-test-w08-in-budapest/ |archive-date=23 May 2019 |access-date=2 August 2017 |website=Mercedes AMG F1}}</ref> He then conducted formal test drives for Mercedes (2017 and 2018)<ref name=":36" /><ref>{{cite web |last=Edmondson |first=Laurence |date=1 August 2018 |title=George Russell puts Mercedes on top on final day of Hungaroring test |url=https://www.espn.co.uk/f1/story/_/id/24255335/george-russell-puts-mercedes-top-final-day-hungaroring-test |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221114201148/https://www.espn.co.uk/f1/story/_/id/24255335/george-russell-puts-mercedes-top-final-day-hungaroring-test |archive-date=14 November 2022 |accessdate=14 November 2022 |website=espn.co.uk}}</ref> and [[Force India]]-Mercedes (2018).<ref>{{Cite web |last=Galloway |first=James |date=11 December 2018 |title=F1 Testing: Max Verstappen sets Barcelona pace for Red Bull |url=https://www.skysports.com/f1/news/12433/11372420/f1-testing-max-verstappen-sets-pace-mercedes-light-up-barcelona |access-date=5 March 2025 |website=Sky Sports |language=en}}</ref>

Russell made his Grand Prix weekend debut at the end of the 2017 season, driving for Force India during free practice at the [[2017 Brazilian Grand Prix|Brazilian]] and [[2017 Abu Dhabi Grand Prix|Abu Dhabi]] Grands Prix.<ref>{{Cite news |date=7 November 2017 |title=British driver George Russell to debut for Force India in Brazilian Grand Prix practice |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/41907080 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190405042636/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/41907080 |archive-date=5 April 2019 |access-date=8 November 2017 |work=BBC Sport}}</ref> Mercedes promoted him to first-team reserve driver in 2018.<ref>{{cite web |last=Larkam |first=Lewis |date=22 February 2018 |title=Wehrlein, Russell to split Mercedes F1 reserve duties in 2018 |url=https://www.crash.net/f1/news/889928/1/wehrlein-russell-split-mercedes-f1-reserve-duties-2018 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221114201149/https://www.crash.net/f1/news/889928/1/wehrlein-russell-split-mercedes-f1-reserve-duties-2018 |archive-date=14 November 2022 |accessdate=14 November 2022 |website=crash.net}}</ref>

===Williams (2019–2021)===
In October 2018, Mercedes arranged for Russell to make his Formula One debut with engine customer [[Williams Racing|Williams]]-Mercedes.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Williams sign Mercedes junior Russell on multi-year deal |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.williams-sign-mercedes-junior-russell-on-multi-year-deal.20FsNkLv60MCmc0IGUkEc4.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210718133634/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.williams-sign-mercedes-junior-russell-on-multi-year-deal.20FsNkLv60MCmc0IGUkEc4.html |archive-date=18 July 2021 |access-date=18 July 2021 |website=Formula1.com}}</ref> Russell had previously applied for a Williams drive after winning the 2017 GP3 title, but Williams's [[Paddy Lowe]] was unmoved by his new PowerPoint presentation and Russell went to Formula 2.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Hudson |first=Henry |date=10 August 2023 |title=Leclerc, Norris and Russell: rise of F1's 'golden generation' profiled in new bios |url=https://www.motorsportmagazine.com/articles/single-seaters/f1/leclerc-norris-and-russell-rise-of-f1s-golden-generation-profiled-in-new-bios/ |access-date=5 March 2025 |website=Motor Sport Magazine |language=en-GB}}</ref> Russell signed a three-year contract with Williams<ref name=":6">{{Cite web |date=15 July 2022 |title=Russell admits that three years with Williams was 'too long' – but says there was 'no way out' {{!}} Formula 1® |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/russell-admits-that-three-years-with-williams-was-too-long-there-was-no-way.784NYfK7ijIOTap4tvZ4Yu |access-date=16 October 2024 |website=Formula 1® - The Official F1® Website}}</ref> but remained a Mercedes test driver.<ref>{{cite web |last=Galloway |first=James |date=4 December 2019 |title=F1 Testing: George Russell fastest for Mercedes on 2019's final day |url=https://www.skysports.com/f1/news/12433/11877971/f1-testing-george-russell-fastest-for-mercedes-on-2019s-final-day |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221114222625/https://www.skysports.com/f1/news/12433/11877971/f1-testing-george-russell-fastest-for-mercedes-on-2019s-final-day |archive-date=14 November 2022 |accessdate=14 November 2022 |website=skysports.com}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |date=2 August 2021 |title=Russell to drive for Mercedes in this week's 2022 tyre test in Hungary |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.russell-to-drive-for-mercedes-in-this-weeks-2022-tyre-test-in-hungary.20GgIeVh7gtJT5JJhcUkUR.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221117191950/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.russell-to-drive-for-mercedes-in-this-weeks-2022-tyre-test-in-hungary.20GgIeVh7gtJT5JJhcUkUR.html |archive-date=17 November 2022 |access-date=17 November 2022 |website=Formula1.com}}</ref> He was partnered by [[Robert Kubica]] for the [[2019 Formula One World Championship|2019 season]]<ref>{{Cite news |date=22 November 2018 |title=Robert Kubica: Polish driver to make F1 comeback with Williams in 2019 |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/46300009 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181122094105/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/46300009 |archive-date=22 November 2018 |access-date=22 November 2018 |work=BBC Sport}}</ref> and [[Nicholas Latifi]] in [[2020 Formula One World Championship|2020]] and [[2021 Formula One World Championship|2021]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=Russell and Latifi to stay on at Williams in unchanged 2021 driver line-up |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.russell-and-latifi-to-stay-on-at-williams-in-unchanged-2021-driver-line-up.2buMT250BE0Ef8Q2bUBDFE.html |access-date=16 July 2020 |website=formula1.com |date=16 July 2020 |archive-date=19 September 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200919002445/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.russell-and-latifi-to-stay-on-at-williams-in-unchanged-2021-driver-line-up.2buMT250BE0Ef8Q2bUBDFE.html |url-status=live}}</ref> His first appearance for Williams was at the 2018 post-season test at [[Yas Marina Circuit]], driving the [[Williams FW41|FW41]].<ref>{{cite web |last=Smith |first=Luke |date=27 November 2018 |title=George Russell pleased with 'very positive' first Williams F1 test |url=https://www.crash.net/f1/news/911329/1/russell-pleased-very-positive-first-williams-f1-test |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181127161037/https://www.crash.net/f1/news/911329/1/russell-pleased-very-positive-first-williams-f1-test |archive-date=27 November 2018 |accessdate=14 November 2018 |website=crash.net}}</ref>

Russell's years at Williams were difficult. Mercedes had hoped that Williams would field a competitive car; as Russell later noted, Williams had finished no worse than fifth in the constructors' standings from {{F1|2015}} to {{F1|2017}}.<ref name=":6" /> However, when Russell joined Williams, the team was well behind the rest of the field<ref>{{Cite web |date=March 2019 |title=Russell accepts Williams slowest despite 'big step' |url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/russell-williams-slowest/4345758/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210718132131/https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/russell-williams-slowest/4345758/ |archive-date=18 July 2021 |access-date=18 July 2021 |website=Motorsport.com}}</ref> and did not produce a car that could reliably compete for points until 2021, Russell's final year with the team. The team was so strapped for cash that it considered replacing Russell with [[Kevin Magnussen]] after the 2020 season if Magnussen could find enough sponsor money to keep the team afloat.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Gamble |first=Andrew |date=6 November 2021 |title=Williams held talks over axing George Russell before Mercedes move |url=https://www.express.co.uk/sport/f1-autosport/1517363/Williams-George-Russell-Mercedes |access-date=20 September 2024 |website=Express.co.uk}}</ref>

Due to Russell's extended run at Williams, he is third on the list of [[List of Formula One driver records#Most races before scoring points|most race starts in a career before scoring points]], with 37. However, the Formula One team principals viewed his performances more favorably. In 2020, a year where Russell scored only three points and finished 18th in the standings,<ref name=":27">{{Cite web |title=2020 Driver Standings |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/results/2020/drivers |access-date=5 March 2025 |website=Formula 1® - The Official F1® Website |language=en}}</ref> the team principals ranked him that year's sixth-best driver.<ref>{{Cite web |title=REVEALED: F1's team bosses choose their Top 10 drivers of 2020 {{!}} Formula 1® |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/revealed-f1s-team-bosses-choose-their-top-10-drivers-of-2020.2z5yo7av41tQC3MrzeFNa3 |access-date=16 October 2024 |website=Formula 1® - The Official F1® Website}}</ref> In addition, Russell led Williams back to respectability in 2021, scoring 16 points and recording a rare podium for Williams.<ref name=":28">{{Cite web |title=2021 Driver Standings |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/results/2021/drivers |access-date=5 March 2025 |website=Formula 1® - The Official F1® Website |language=en}}</ref>

==== 2019–2020: Rookie season and first points ====
[[File:George Russell Mugello 2020, race day.jpg|thumb|Russell at the [[2020 Tuscan Grand Prix]], where he finished 11th]]
In 2019, Williams struggled for form. At Russell's Formula One race debut, the {{F1 GP|2019|Australian}}, Russell qualified 19th and finished 16th.<ref>{{Cite web |date=17 March 2019 |title=Australian Grand Prix |url=https://www.williamsf1.com/racing/news/2019/03/australian-grand-prix |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190323111815/https://www.williamsf1.com/racing/news/2019/03/australian-grand-prix |archive-date=23 March 2019 |access-date=19 February 2025 |website=[[Williams Racing]]}}</ref> He acknowledged that his experience was difficult, remarking that the car was "four seconds off the pace" and that he was lapped multiple times.<ref name=":25">{{Cite AV media |url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GBqSXuAl3CI |title=Top Drivers on Their First Formula 1 Race {{!}} Lando Norris, George Russell, Ollie Bearman & Alex Albon |date=27 February 2025 |last=High Performance |access-date=5 March 2025 |via=YouTube}} (22:05-25:39)</ref> Williams's slow pace continued into the season, and in most races Kubica was Russell's only on-track competition: Russell did not finish ahead of a car from another team until round six, the {{F1 GP|2019|Monaco}}. He also outqualified Kubica at all twenty-one races.<ref>{{cite web |last=Galloway |first=James |date=30 November 2019 |title=F1 2019 qualifying match-ups: Lando Norris finishes ahead at McLaren |url=https://www.skysports.com/f1/news/12433/11874648/f1-2019-qualifying-match-ups-lando-norris-finishes-ahead-at-mclaren |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221114221440/https://www.skysports.com/f1/news/12433/11874648/f1-2019-qualifying-match-ups-lando-norris-finishes-ahead-at-mclaren |archive-date=14 November 2022 |accessdate=14 November 2022 |website=skysports.com}}</ref>

Russell's best placement was 11th at the rain-affected {{F1 GP|2019|German}}, where Williams rolled out an upgrade,<ref>{{Cite web |date=1 August 2019 |title=Kubica had 'mixed feelings' after scoring point as he predicts tough weekend in Hungary |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/kubica-had-mixed-feelings-after-scoring-hockenheim-point-as-he-predicts.5uY9VwdUMAYO5aPUYRApgN |access-date=5 March 2025 |website=Formula 1® - The Official F1® Website |language=en}}</ref> six cars retired without classifying,<ref>{{Cite web |date=8 August 2019 |title=Russell hails 'best weekend of the year' in Hungary after 'absolute disaster' in Germany {{!}} Formula 1® |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/russell-hails-hungary-best-weekend-of-the-year-after-disaster-of-germany.XTIJ2pBeqo8PKnpX6bzU5 |access-date=5 March 2025 |website=Formula 1® - The Official F1® Website |language=en}}</ref> and another two cars received time penalties after the race.<ref name=":26">{{Cite web |title=What the teams said - Race day in Germany {{!}} Formula 1® |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/what-the-teams-said-race-day-in-germany-2019.6HeoWvqoqsKvmPTD6tv9ss |access-date=5 March 2025 |website=Formula 1® - The Official F1® Website |language=en}}</ref> He came close to finishing tenth, but unsuccessfully asked to pit for slick tyres during a safety car and ran wide on turn two several laps later,<ref>{{Cite web |last=Collantine |first=Keith |date=30 July 2019 |title="I think it's slicks, mate": How Russell missed his first chance for points |url=https://www.racefans.net/2019/07/30/i-think-its-slicks-mate-how-russell-missed-his-first-chance-for-points/ |access-date=5 March 2025 |website=RaceFans |language=en-GB}}</ref> allowing Kubica to overtake him and score the team's only point that year.<ref name=":26" /> In 2023, Russell remarked that it was the most disappointing moment of his career.<ref>''Rookies Reunited'' (2023), at 7:20-8:17.</ref> Russell also finished 12th at the {{F1 GP|2019|Brazilian}} after a late safety car allowed him to unlap himself, missing out on points by 1.668 seconds.<ref>{{Cite web |date=19 November 2019 |title='It wasn't meant to be' - Russell on missing maiden point by 1.6s {{!}} Formula 1® |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/it-wasnt-meant-to-be-russell-on-missing-maiden-point-by-1-6s.6H2tGBFFgKV82JkqxbiFFX |access-date=5 March 2025 |website=Formula 1® - The Official F1® Website |language=en}}</ref> He finished 20th in the Drivers' Championship, scoring no points to Kubica's one.<ref>{{Cite web |title=2019 Driver Standings |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/results.html/2019/drivers.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190526191916/https://www.formula1.com/en/results.html/2019/drivers.html |archive-date=26 May 2019 |access-date=18 July 2021 |website=Formula 1}}</ref> Russell later remarked that as a competitor, it was hard for him to watch fellow rookies [[Alex Albon]] and [[Lando Norris]] competing for points and podiums after beating them the year before in F2.<ref name=":25" />

Williams was more competitive on track in 2020, but it did not show up in the standings, as Williams did not score any points all year.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Horton |first=Phillip |date=28 December 2020 |title=Williams' year-on-year gains 'remarkable' – Latifi |url=https://www.motorsportweek.com/2020/12/28/williams-year-on-year-gains-remarkable-latifi/ |access-date=5 March 2025 |website=Motorsport Week |language=en-GB}}</ref> However, Russell came close to scoring on several occasions, such as the {{F1 GP|2020|Styrian}} (starting 11th but falling to 16th after running into the gravel during a re-start lap)<ref>{{Cite web |date=12 July 2020 |title=Styrian Grand Prix 2020 race report and highlights: Lewis Hamilton eases to Styrian Grand Prix victory over Bottas as Ferraris collide |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/hamilton-eases-to-styrian-grand-prix-victory-over-bottas-as-ferraris-collide.5PfZ0DxltY7qOrbeVXMLa3 |access-date=5 March 2025 |website=Formula 1® - The Official F1® Website |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=13 July 2020 |title='I messed up' admits George Russell after Lap 4 off in Styrian GP – but says 'slow' Williams was bigger problem {{!}} Formula 1®' |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.i-messed-up-admits-russell-after-lap-4-off-in-styrian-gp-but-says-slow-car.629eTPbqmQWg0ynbcFjbEk.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210718132130/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.i-messed-up-admits-russell-after-lap-4-off-in-styrian-gp-but-says-slow-car.629eTPbqmQWg0ynbcFjbEk.html |archive-date=18 July 2021 |access-date=18 July 2021 |website=Formula1.com}}</ref> the {{F1 GP|2020|British}} (finishing 12th), the {{F1 GP|2020|Tuscan}} (reaching 9th at one point before dropping back to 11th),<ref>{{cite web |date=13 September 2020 |title=Tuscan GP: George Russell denied first Formula 1 points in cruel finish |url=https://www.skysports.com/f1/news/36305/12071330/tuscan-gp-george-russell-denied-first-formula-1-points-in-cruel-finish |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200918015258/https://www.skysports.com/f1/news/36305/12071330/tuscan-gp-george-russell-denied-first-formula-1-points-in-cruel-finish |archive-date=18 September 2020 |access-date=7 October 2020 |website=skysports.com}}</ref> and the {{F1 GP|2020|Emilia Romagna}} (crashing out from tenth place under safety car conditions).<ref>{{Cite web|title=Russell: Imola F1 safety car crash the biggest mistake of my career|url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/russell-imola-f1-safety-car-crash-the-biggest-mistake-of-my-career-4977629/4977629/|access-date=18 July 2021|website=Autosport.com|date=2 November 2020|archive-date=18 July 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210718132136/https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/russell-imola-f1-safety-car-crash-the-biggest-mistake-of-my-career-4977629/4977629/|url-status=live}}</ref>

<!-- Deleted image removed: [[File:George Russell 2020 Sakhir Grand Prix.jpg|thumb|left|Russell made a surprise debut for [[Mercedes-Benz in Formula One|Mercedes]] at the {{F1GP|2020|Sakhir}} in {{F1|2020}}, where he led the majority of the race.|alt=Russell leads Valtteri Bottas in the Mercedes W11 at the 2020 Sakhir Grand Prix]] -->
Russell scored his first points at the {{F1 GP|2020|Sakhir}}, following a surprise promotion to the Mercedes senior team when [[Lewis Hamilton]] tested positive for [[COVID-19]].<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.mercedesamgf1.com/en/news/2020/2020-sakhir-grand-prix/2020-sakhir-grand-prix-reserve-driver-announcement/|title=Mercedes Confirms George Russell for Sakhir GP|website=Mercedesamgf1.com|access-date=2 December 2020|archive-date=2 December 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201202074256/https://www.mercedesamgf1.com/en/news/2020/2020-sakhir-grand-prix/2020-sakhir-grand-prix-reserve-driver-announcement/|url-status=live}}</ref> His performance at Sakhir was widely acclaimed by both Mercedes and the media.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Brundle |first=Martin |author-link=Martin Brundle |date=8 December 2020 |title=Martin Brundle: Sergio Perez, George Russell and the story of a dramatic Sakhir GP |url=https://www.skysports.com/f1/news/24096/12154973/martin-brundle-sergio-perez-george-russell-and-the-story-of-a-dramatic-sakhir-gp |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201208224618/https://www.skysports.com/f1/news/24096/12154973/martin-brundle-sergio-perez-george-russell-and-the-story-of-a-dramatic-sakhir-gp |archive-date=8 December 2020 |access-date=9 December 2020 |website=[[Sky Sports]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last=Cooper |first=Adam |date=8 December 2020 |title=Mercedes impressed by how Russell handled F1 pressure |url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/mercedes-impressed-by-how-attacking-russell-handled-pressure/4923546/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220615153151/https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/mercedes-impressed-by-how-attacking-russell-handled-pressure/4923546/ |archive-date=15 June 2022 |access-date=11 April 2022 |website=Motorsport.com}}</ref> He narrowly missed out on pole position,<ref>{{Cite web |date=5 December 2020 |title=F1 2020 Sakhir Grand Prix - Full Qualifying Results |url=https://www.crash.net/f1/results/949884/1/f1-2020-sakhir-grand-prix-full-qualifying-results |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210718132131/https://www.crash.net/f1/results/949884/1/f1-2020-sakhir-grand-prix-full-qualifying-results |archive-date=18 July 2021 |access-date=18 July 2021 |website=Crash}}</ref> overtook teammate [[Valtteri Bottas]] at the first corner, and led the majority of the race. However, he was forced to pit twice in-a-row when the Mercedes pit crew accidentally fitted Bottas's front tyres on his car, following a radio failure.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Mercedes handed €20,000 fine for Russell tyre mix-up in Sakhir Grand Prix |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.mercedes-handed-eur20-000-fine-for-russell-tyre-mix-up-in-sakhir-grand-prix.3PwKTGxftR3C8ACA5DcDKj.html|access-date=18 July 2021|website=Formula1.com|archive-date=25 May 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210525200351/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.mercedes-handed-eur20-000-fine-for-russell-tyre-mix-up-in-sakhir-grand-prix.3PwKTGxftR3C8ACA5DcDKj.html|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |date=7 December 2020 |title=George Russell 'gutted' as Mercedes debut Sakhir GP win is 'taken away' |url=https://www.skysports.com/f1/news/36305/12153661/george-russell-gutted-as-mercedes-sakhir-gp-win-is-taken-away |access-date=6 September 2024 |work=Sky Sports}}</ref> He overtook Bottas a second time, recovered to second place, and was closing in on race leader [[Sergio Pérez]], when a puncture forced him to pit again with ten laps to go.<ref>{{Cite web|title=2020 Sakhir Grand Prix: Late puncture costs Russell podium place|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/video.2020-sakhir-grand-prix-late-puncture-costs-russell-podium-place.1687521520283184367.html|access-date=18 July 2021|website=Formula1.com|archive-date=18 July 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210718133637/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/video.2020-sakhir-grand-prix-late-puncture-costs-russell-podium-place.1687521520283184367.html|url-status=live}}</ref> He finished ninth, picking up two points for the finish and one point for the fastest lap.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/russell-losing-victory-twice-in-bahrain-really-bloody-hurts/4922790/|title=George Russell: Losing Bahrain F1 victory twice really hurts|website=Motorsport.com|date=6 December 2020 |access-date=8 December 2020|archive-date=7 December 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201207020454/https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/russell-losing-victory-twice-in-bahrain-really-bloody-hurts/4922790/|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=6 December 2020 |title=Sergio Perez takes sensational maiden win in Sakhir GP as tyre mix-up ruins Russell's charge |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.sergio-perez-takes-sensational-maiden-win-in-sakhir-gp-as-tyre-issues-ruin.2TBf7rg5wpgELNALXJLRHV.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201207063434/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.sergio-perez-takes-sensational-maiden-win-in-sakhir-gp-as-tyre-issues-ruin.2TBf7rg5wpgELNALXJLRHV.html |archive-date=7 December 2020 |access-date=8 December 2020 |website=Formula1.com}}</ref> He later remarked that while "I was the same driver [in Sakhir] as I had been before ... I was exactly the same driver a week later [driving for Williams at the season-ending {{F1 GP|2020|Abu Dhabi}}<ref name=":1">{{Cite web |title=Hamilton to make Mercedes return in Abu Dhabi after testing Covid-negative, with Russell heading back to Williams |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.hamilton-to-make-mercedes-return-in-abu-dhabi-after-testing-covid-negative.6crMz5aWmfElFkpMdTpLwL.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201210174506/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.hamilton-to-make-mercedes-return-in-abu-dhabi-after-testing-covid-negative.6crMz5aWmfElFkpMdTpLwL.html |archive-date=10 December 2020 |access-date=10 December 2020 |website=Formula1.com}}</ref>] when I was out in Q1."<ref>{{Cite book |last=Whyman |first=Matt |url=https://books.google.com/books?id=1koSEQAAQBAJ |title=Inside Mercedes F1: Life in the Fast Lane |date=12 November 2024 |publisher=Crown |isbn=978-0-593-73564-0 |pages=32 |language=en}}</ref> In Abu Dhabi, he donned a special helmet to honor the Williams family, who had sold the team in October.<ref>{{Cite web |date=11 December 2020 |title=Russell to wear Williams tribute helmet for Abu Dhabi GP. |url=https://www.motorsportweek.com/2020/12/11/russell-to-wear-williams-tribute-helmet-for-abu-dhabi-gp/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201211085234/https://www.motorsportweek.com/2020/12/11/russell-to-wear-williams-tribute-helmet-for-abu-dhabi-gp/ |archive-date=11 December 2020 |access-date=18 July 2021 |website=Motorsportweek.com}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Shah |first=Kunal |date=30 October 2020 |title=Sir Frank & Claire Williams Both Leave Roles At Legendary F1 Team |url=https://www.kunalsf1blog.com/frank-claire-williams-leave-team/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210718132133/https://www.kunalsf1blog.com/frank-claire-williams-leave-team/ |archive-date=18 July 2021 |access-date=18 July 2021 |website=Kunal's F1 Blog}}</ref> He finished 18th in the Drivers' Championship, scoring three points, all for Mercedes.<ref name=":27" />

====2021: Maiden podium====
Following Russell's strong performances in 2020, Mercedes looked into finding him a new team for the [[2021 Formula One World Championship|2021 season]], but Williams declined to release him from his contract.<ref name=":6" /> In addition, the media speculated that he would replace [[Valtteri Bottas]] at Mercedes in 2022 once their respective contracts expired. The two aspirants clashed at the 2021 {{F1 GP|2021|Emilia Romagna}}, when Russell found himself alongside Bottas on lap 30. He attempted to overtake Bottas, but drove onto a wet patch and lost control of his car, crashing into Bottas and causing a double retirement.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Herbert |first=Danny |date=19 April 2021 |title=Russell and Bottas crash analysis |url=https://drivetribe.com/p/russell-and-bottas-crash-analysis-DUpm07EeT7C8THxciAzozQ |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220122153611/https://drivetribe.com/p/russell-and-bottas-crash-analysis-DUpm07EeT7C8THxciAzozQ |archive-date=22 January 2022 |access-date=18 July 2021 |website=DriveTribe}}</ref> Russell initially blamed the incident on Bottas, walking over to Bottas after the crash and slapping his helmet (Bottas responded with a middle finger), and accusing him of "trying to kill [them] both".<ref>{{cite web |date=18 April 2021 |title=George Russell and Valtteri Bottas crash: Drivers blame each other for causing 'dangerous' Imola collision |url=https://www.skysports.com/f1/news/12433/12279561/george-russell-and-valtteri-bottas-crash-drivers-blame-each-other-for-causing-dangerous-imola-collision |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210418235403/https://www.skysports.com/f1/news/12433/12279561/george-russell-and-valtteri-bottas-crash-drivers-blame-each-other-for-causing-dangerous-imola-collision |archive-date=18 April 2021 |access-date=18 April 2021 |website=[[Sky Sports]]}}</ref> However, Russell later retracted his claims and apologised to Bottas and Williams.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Noble |first=Jonathan |date=19 April 2021 |title=Russell apologises to Bottas after Imola incident |url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/russell-apologises-to-bottas-imola-incident/6350886/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210423065857/https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/russell-apologises-to-bottas-imola-incident/6350886/ |archive-date=23 April 2021 |access-date=23 April 2021 |website=motorsport.com}}</ref> Mercedes boss [[Toto Wolff]] acknowledged that Bottas should not have been side by side with a Williams in the first place, but reserved the bulk of his criticism for Russell, a Mercedes junior who had just taken out a Mercedes.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Richards |first=Giles |date=19 April 2021 |title=Toto Wolff rebukes George Russell over Imola F1 crash with Valtteri Bottas |url=https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2021/apr/19/toto-wolff-george-russell-imola-crash-valtteri-bottas-mercedes-williams-f1 |access-date=16 October 2024 |work=The Guardian |issn=0261-3077}}</ref> Both drivers sought to downplay the dispute, at least publicly, after Bottas rejoined Mercedes in {{F1|2025}}.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Medland |first=Chris |date=31 January 2025 |title=Russell sees 2025 as the start of a new career chapter as Mercedes' experienced driver |url=https://racer.com/2025/01/31/russell-sees-2025-as-the-start-of-a-new-career-chapter-as-mercedes-experienced-driver/ |access-date=17 February 2025 |website=RACER |language=en-US |archive-date=16 February 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250216081015/https://racer.com/2025/01/31/russell-sees-2025-as-the-start-of-a-new-career-chapter-as-mercedes-experienced-driver/ |url-status=dead }}</ref><ref>{{Cite AV media |url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hAw_G3SF6Fk |title=Valtteri Bottas opens up on his role at Mercedes this season |date=10 February 2025 |last=((Sky Sports F1)) |access-date=17 February 2025 |via=YouTube}}</ref>[[File:FIA F1 Austria 2021 Nr. 63 Russell.jpg|thumb|left|Russell at the [[2021 Austrian Grand Prix]]. He finished 11th, but received praise from Fernando Alonso for his performance.]]

Despite his DNF at Imola, Russell helped Williams to its best season in several years. He came close to scoring points at a number of races, including the {{F1 GP|2021|Azerbaijan}} (gearbox failure following a restart in 15th place);<ref>{{Cite web|title=2021 Azerbaijan Grand Prix|url=https://www.williamsf1.com/news/2021/races/baku/azerbaijan-grand-prix|access-date=18 July 2021|website=Williamsf1.com|archive-date=18 July 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210718132132/https://www.williamsf1.com/news/2021/races/baku/azerbaijan-grand-prix|url-status=live}}</ref> the {{F1 GP|2021|French}} (rising from 19th to 12th without help from driver retirements);<ref>{{cite web |date=21 June 2021 |title=Russell says French Grand Prix was 'best race I've ever had with Williams' |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.russell-says-french-grand-prix-was-best-race-ive-ever-had-with-williams.1oC8lQBKhGuaADc8I8xjqK.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210710104354/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.russell-says-french-grand-prix-was-best-race-ive-ever-had-with-williams.1oC8lQBKhGuaADc8I8xjqK.html |archive-date=10 July 2021 |access-date=26 June 2021 |website=formula1.com}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Kelly |first=Sean |date=20 June 2021 |title=French GP Facts & Stats: Verstappen's first F1 hat-trick, and a special podium for Perez |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.french-gp-facts-and-stats-verstappens-first-f1-hat-trick-and-a-special.5RdIdqVagUjxZf5rQ3VASt.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210621003951/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.french-gp-facts-and-stats-verstappens-first-f1-hat-trick-and-a-special.5RdIdqVagUjxZf5rQ3VASt.html |archive-date=21 June 2021 |access-date=20 June 2021 |website=Formula1.com}}</ref> the {{F1 GP|2021|Styrian}} (hydraulic failure after qualifying in tenth);<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.skysports.com/f1/news/36606/12342547/styrian-gp-yuki-tsunoda-grid-drop-for-valtteri-bottas-block-moves-george-russell-into-top-10|title=Yuki Tsunoda grid drop for Valtteri Bottas block moves George Russell into top 10|website=[[Sky Sports]]|date=27 June 2021|access-date=26 June 2021|archive-date=26 June 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210626235649/https://www.skysports.com/f1/news/36606/12342547/styrian-gp-yuki-tsunoda-grid-drop-for-valtteri-bottas-block-moves-george-russell-into-top-10|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://us.motorsport.com/f1/news/russell-rues-typical-bad-luck-after-styrian-gp-retirement/6615160/|title=Russell rues "typical" bad luck after Styrian GP Retirement|website=[[Motorsport.com]]|date=27 June 2021|access-date=27 June 2021|archive-date=30 June 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210630202411/https://us.motorsport.com/f1/news/russell-rues-typical-bad-luck-after-styrian-gp-retirement/6615160/|url-status=live}}</ref> and the {{F1 GP|2021|British}} (12th place). At the {{F1 GP|2021|Austrian}}, Russell qualified in eighth place, Williams's highest grid position since 2017.<ref>{{Cite web|title=2021 Austrian Grand Prix qualifying facts and stats: McLaren secure first front row start for almost a decade|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.austrian-gp-qualifying-facts-and-stats-mclaren-secure-first-front-row-start.1zuvvwLS7n6VGNkcU43KIc.html|url-status=live|access-date=4 July 2021|website=Formula1.com|archive-date=5 July 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210705010218/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.austrian-gp-qualifying-facts-and-stats-mclaren-secure-first-front-row-start.1zuvvwLS7n6VGNkcU43KIc.html}}</ref><ref name="VettelPenalty">{{Cite web|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.breaking-vettel-handed-3-place-grid-drop-for-impeding-alonso-in-qualifying.7GgtvflZ8oncSBvUpU34UU.html|title=Vettel handed 3-place grid drop for impeding Alonso in qualifying|website=Formula1.com|date=3 July 2021|access-date=3 July 2021|archive-date=11 July 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210711214845/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.breaking-vettel-handed-3-place-grid-drop-for-impeding-alonso-in-qualifying.7GgtvflZ8oncSBvUpU34UU.html|url-status=live}}</ref> He was still in tenth near the end of the race, but after a fourteen-lap defensive battle, [[Fernando Alonso]] passed him with three laps to go.<ref name=":29">{{Cite news |last=Benson |first=Andrew |date=7 September 2021 |title=George Russell: Why Mercedes had to sign him - and what it might mean for team harmony |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/formula1/58457633 |access-date=5 March 2025 |work=BBC Sport |language=en-GB}}</ref><ref name=":4">{{Cite AV media |url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LJwSs6UgNB8 |title=Alonso and Russell's Epic Duel {{!}} 2021 Austrian Grand Prix |date=5 July 2021 |last=((FORMULA 1)) |access-date=16 October 2024 |via=YouTube}}</ref> After the race, Alonso consoled Russell with a hug.<ref name=":4" /> The Spaniard ruefully explained that "I was hoping it was anyone but him. ... He will have more opportunities hopefully for podiums or wins in the future."<ref>{{Cite news |date=4 July 2021 |title=Alonso feels for Russell after snatching a point in Austria |url=https://www.reuters.com/lifestyle/sports/alonso-feels-russell-after-snatching-point-austria-2021-07-04/ |access-date=15 October 2024 |work=Reuters}}</ref>

Russell scored his first points for Williams two races later at the {{F1 GP|2021|Hungarian}}, moving from 17th on the grid to eighth.<ref>{{Cite web |title=George Russell says he 'shed a tear' after sealing his first-ever points for Williams in Hungary {{!}} Formula 1® |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/russell-says-he-shed-a-tear-after-sealing-his-first-ever-points-for-williams.4UWCveALLJIEVbEGaXP8wr |access-date=16 October 2024 |website=Formula 1® - The Official F1® Website}}</ref> Following the race, Mercedes agreed to promote Russell to the senior team for the 2022 season.<ref>{{Cite web |title='It Was a Dream Come True' - George Recalls F1 Debut Five Years On |url=https://www.mercedesamgf1.com/news/it-was-a-dream-come-true-george-recalls-f1-debut-five-years-on |access-date=5 March 2025 |website=Mercedes-AMG PETRONAS F1 Team |language=en-US}}</ref> In the very next race, Russell collected his maiden podium at the {{F1 GP|2021|Belgian}} under unusual circumstances. He qualified in second after a rain-affected Saturday, the first front-row start for Williams since the [[2017 Italian Grand Prix]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.qualifying-verstappen-denies-russell-shock-pole-in-dramatic-wet-qualifying.XP92uMlcsG9ZQbF0vpqYn.html|title=QUALIFYING: Verstappen denies Russell shock pole in dramatic wet qualifying session at Spa|website=formula1.com|date=28 August 2021|accessdate=28 August 2021|archive-date=28 August 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210828152920/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.qualifying-verstappen-denies-russell-shock-pole-in-dramatic-wet-qualifying.XP92uMlcsG9ZQbF0vpqYn.html|url-status=live}}</ref> The downpour continued into race day, so the race director ran the race for two laps under safety car conditions before calling it off, handing Russell his first Formula One podium finish.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.skysports.com/f1/news/36305/12394797/belgian-gp-george-russell-embraces-strange-first-f1-podium-as-qualifying-heroics-count|title=Belgian GP: George Russell embraces 'strange' first F1 podium as qualifying heroics count|website=skysports.com|date=29 August 2021|accessdate=30 August 2021|archive-date=29 August 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210829210140/https://www.skysports.com/f1/news/36305/12394797/belgian-gp-george-russell-embraces-strange-first-f1-podium-as-qualifying-heroics-count|url-status=live}}</ref> It was Williams's only podium finish between the [[2017 Azerbaijan Grand Prix|2017]] and [[2025 Azerbaijan Grand Prix|2025 Azerbaijan Grands Prix]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Edmondson |first=Laurence |date=22 September 2025 |title=Baku podium sets record straight on Sainz's Williams season |url=https://www.espn.com/racing/f1/story/_/id/46345403/carlos-sainz-baku-grand-prix-williams-formula-one-analysis |access-date=27 October 2025 |website=ESPN.com |language=en}}</ref> Russell also scored points at the {{F1 GP|2021|Italian}} (ninth) and the {{F1 GP|2021|Russian}} (tenth, after qualifying in third).<ref>{{Cite web|date=27 September 2021|title=Russell says converting P3 grid slot to Russian GP podium was 'not realistic' after claiming P10 in Sochi|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.russell-says-converting-p3-grid-slot-to-russian-gp-podium-was-not-realistic.1pr9J0KV1XNNtDMdRuDofA.html|url-status=live|access-date=27 September 2021|website=Formula1.com|archive-date=27 September 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210927090919/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.russell-says-converting-p3-grid-slot-to-russian-gp-podium-was-not-realistic.1pr9J0KV1XNNtDMdRuDofA.html}}</ref> He placed 15th in the Drivers' Championship, scoring 16 points to Latifi's seven.<ref name=":28" />
{{clear}}

===Mercedes (2022–present)===
[[File:2022 French Grand Prix (52279069978).png|thumb|Russell during the drivers' parade at the [[2022 French Grand Prix]]]]Russell joined Mercedes in [[2022 Formula One World Championship|2022]].<ref name=":2">{{Cite web |date=7 September 2021 |title=Mercedes announce George Russell will partner Lewis Hamilton in 2022 as Briton signs long-term deal |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.mercedes-announce-george-russell-will-partner-lewis-hamilton-in-2022.jtndbCmN3CR8Lm9s54e4T.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210907090616/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.mercedes-announce-george-russell-will-partner-lewis-hamilton-in-2022.jtndbCmN3CR8Lm9s54e4T.html |archive-date=7 September 2021 |access-date=7 September 2021 |website=Formula1.com}}</ref> From 2022 to 2024, he was paired with seven-time World Drivers' Champion [[Lewis Hamilton]].<ref name=":0">{{Cite web |title=Hamilton reveals the key factors behind his Ferrari switch |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/the-stars-aligned-hamilton-reveals-the-key-factors-behind-his-shock-ferrari.2vJRwYdyFN1J3vyTUqZMFr |access-date=30 November 2024 |website=Formula 1® - The Official F1® Website}}</ref> The team placed third in 2022, second in 2023, and fourth in 2024.<ref name=":0" /> Hamilton left at the end of the 2024 season and was succeeded by [[Mercedes Junior Team|Junior Team]] member [[Kimi Antonelli]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=31 August 2024 |title=Antonelli confirmed as Hamilton's replacement with Mercedes looking ahead to 'next chapter' |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/breaking-kimi-antonelli-confirmed-as-lewis-hamiltons-replacement-with.2TeU01Qm9BjQUlBjl9jBTm |access-date=31 August 2024 |website=Formula 1}}</ref>

==== 2022–2023: Maiden win and pole position ====
The timing of Russell's move to Mercedes was unfortunate, as it coincided with a regulations change that ended Mercedes's dominance of the sport.<ref name=":43">{{Cite news |last=Smith |first=Luke |date=25 April 2025 |title=Out of Lewis Hamilton's shadow at Mercedes, George Russell feels ready to be F1 champion |url=https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/6305394/2025/04/25/george-russell-mercedes-top-driver-f1-lewis-hamilton/ |access-date=25 April 2025 |work=The Athletic |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331}}</ref> Mercedes's new aerodynamics concept performed very well in simulations but was difficult to drive in real life.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Hughes |first=Mark |date=17 May 2023 |title=Why Mercedes has got F1's current era so wrong so far |url=https://www.the-race.com/formula-1/why-mercedes-has-got-f1s-current-era-so-wrong-so-far/ |access-date=9 December 2024 |website=The Race}}</ref> The team scored one victory in the first two years of the ground effect era.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Wood |first=Will |date=4 May 2024 |title=Mercedes swapped one extreme for another with 2024 car design - Russell |url=https://www.racefans.net/2024/05/05/mercedes-swapped-one-extreme-for-another-with-2024-car-design-russell/ |access-date=9 December 2024 |website=RaceFans}}</ref>
[[File:2022 British Grand Prix (52382355276).jpg|thumb|left|Russell at the [[2022 British Grand Prix]]. Russell achieved his maiden victory at the [[2022 São Paulo Grand Prix|São Paulo Grand Prix]].]]
Russell and Hamilton spent the first nine races of the 2022 season testing experimental parts for the Mercedes car.<ref name="TheRace222">{{Cite web |date=24 October 2022 |title=What a winless Hamilton season won't tell you about his 2022 |url=https://the-race.com/formula-1/what-a-winless-hamilton-season-wont-tell-you-about-his-2022/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230326200252/https://the-race.com/formula-1/what-a-winless-hamilton-season-wont-tell-you-about-his-2022/ |archive-date=26 March 2023 |access-date=26 March 2023 |website=The Race}}</ref> Although the drivers swapped testing duties every race,<ref>{{Cite news |last=Kalinauckas |first=Alex |date=21 January 2023 |title=Russell sees no risk of Hamilton trouble even amid F1 title battle |url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/russell-sees-no-risk-of-hamilton-trouble-even-amid-f1-title-battle/10423174/ |access-date=9 December 2024 |work=Autosport}}</ref> Russell accumulated a 34-point lead over Hamilton after round nine,<ref>{{Cite web |last=Chiu |first=Nigel |date=19 June 2022 |title=F1 Standings after 2022 Canadian GP |url=https://www.total-motorsport.com/f1-standings-after-2022-canadian-gp/ |access-date=10 December 2024 |website=Total Motorsport |language=}}</ref> which team boss [[Toto Wolff]] attributed to Hamilton's experiments backfiring.<ref>{{Cite web |last1=Collantine |first1=Keith |last2=Cottingham |first2=Claire |date=11 June 2022 |title=Hamilton's recent deficit to Russell is due to 'set-up experiments', says Wolff |url=https://www.racefans.net/2022/06/11/hamiltons-recent-deficit-to-russell-is-due-to-set-up-experiments-says-wolff/ |access-date=9 December 2024 |website=RaceFans}}</ref> After round nine, Russell and Hamilton finished out the season essentially level on points, with Russell scoring one more point than his teammate.<ref name=":17" /> Despite the unfortunate season, Russell checked off several career firsts in 2022, including his first podium in a full-length race at [[2022 Australian Grand Prix|Melbourne]];<ref>{{Cite web |date=10 April 2022 |title=Standings |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/results.html |access-date=10 April 2022 |website=Formula 1 |archive-date=28 October 2014 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20141028202800/http://www.formula1.com/results/driver/2001/40.html |url-status=live }}</ref> his first pole position at [[2022 Hungarian Grand Prix|Hungary]];<ref>{{Cite web |title=Russell beats Sainz to take shock maiden pole at Hungaroring as Red Bulls hit trouble |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.mercedes-take-their-first-pole-position-of-2022-as-russell-sets-the-pace-in.6Vqx91758duUbTENjFUaU0.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220730162413/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.mercedes-take-their-first-pole-position-of-2022-as-russell-sets-the-pace-in.6Vqx91758duUbTENjFUaU0.html |archive-date=30 July 2022 |access-date=30 July 2022 |website=Formula1.com}}</ref> and his first Grand Prix and sprint race victories at [[2022 São Paulo Grand Prix|Interlagos]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Benson |first=Andrew |date=13 November 2022 |title=Sao Paulo Grand Prix: George Russell beats Lewis Hamilton to first full Formula 1 win |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/63617916 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221113215610/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/63617916 |archive-date=13 November 2022 |access-date=14 November 2022 |website=[[BBC Sport]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Benson |first=Andrew |date=12 November 2022 |title=Sao Paulo Grand Prix sprint: George Russell takes first win |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/63610213 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221113220202/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/63610213 |archive-date=13 November 2022 |access-date=14 November 2022 |website=[[BBC Sport]]}}</ref> He finished fourth in the Drivers' Championship, outscoring teammate Hamilton by 35 points.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Larkam |first=Lewis |date=2 December 2022 |title=George Russell reveals reason for Lewis Hamilton's early F1 2022 car experiments: 'I was in a happier place' {{!}} F1 {{!}} Crash |url=https://www.crash.net/f1/news/1018065/1/russell-reveals-reason-hamilton-s-early-f1-2022-experiments |access-date=16 October 2024 |website=www.crash.net}}</ref><ref name=":17">{{Cite web |last=Collantine |first=Keith |date=2 December 2022 |title=Did Russell deserve to out-score Hamilton? Perhaps not - but it was close |url=https://www.racefans.net/2022/12/02/did-russell-deserve-to-out-score-hamilton-perhaps-not-but-it-was-close/ |access-date=16 October 2024 |website=RaceFans}}</ref>
[[File:FIA F1 Austria 2023 Nr. 63 (1).jpg|thumb|Russell at the [[2023 Austrian Grand Prix]]]]
{{F1|2023}} was another difficult year for Mercedes and for Russell in particular. After some promising performances at the start of the season (leading the {{F1 GP|2023|Australian}} until an untimely red flag<ref>{{Cite news |date=2 April 2023 |title='It's just such a shame' says Mercedes' Russell after retiring with power unit issue in Australia |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.its-just-such-a-shame-says-mercedes-russell-after-retiring-with-power-unit.1BhfnePPs7NbkXPJg5yOc1.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230403193314/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.its-just-such-a-shame-says-mercedes-russell-after-retiring-with-power-unit.1BhfnePPs7NbkXPJg5yOc1.html |archive-date=3 April 2023 |access-date=5 April 2023 |work=Formula 1}}</ref> and scoring a podium at [[2023 Spanish Grand Prix|Barcelona]]<ref>{{Cite news |last=Cleeren |first=Filip |date= |title=Russell: Double F1 podium "a sign of things to come" for Mercedes |url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/russell-double-podium-a-sign-of-things-to-come-for-mercedes-f1/10478604/ |access-date=10 June 2023 |work=Motorsport.com}}</ref>), Russell's results declined in the second half of the season for a variety of reasons, including a record seven pit stops in one race ([[2023 Dutch Grand Prix|Zandvoort]]),<ref name=":13">{{Cite web |last= |date=28 November 2023 |title=2023 Formula 1: Records and milestones, more than 40 of them! |url=https://www.grandprix247.com/2023/11/28/2023-formula-1-records-and-milestones-more-than-40-of-them/ |access-date=16 October 2024 |website=GRANDPRIX247}}</ref> an accidental last-lap crash ([[2023 Singapore Grand Prix|Singapore]]),<ref>{{cite web |date=17 September 2023 |title=Sainz holds off Norris and fast-charging Mercedes pair to take sensational Singapore Grand Prix victory |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.sainz-holds-off-norris-and-fast-charging-mercedes-pair-to-take-sensational.16sNsRUz2MAFyXxSE3RdwX.html |accessdate=17 September 2023 |website=formula1.com}}</ref> an over-aggressive strategy call ([[2023 Japanese Grand Prix|Suzuka]]),<ref name=":5">{{cite web |date=25 September 2023 |title=Lewis Hamilton and George Russell explain dramatic Japanese GP for Mercedes as pair come close to contact at Suzuka |url=https://www.skysports.com/f1/news/12433/12968648/lewis-hamilton-and-george-russell-explain-dramatic-japanese-gp-for-mercedes-as-pair-come-close-to-contact-at-suzuka |accessdate=12 November 2023 |website=skysports.com}}</ref> and Hamilton colliding into him after a front-row start ([[2023 Qatar Grand Prix|Lusail]]).<ref>{{cite web |last=Galloway |first=James |date=9 October 2023 |title=Lewis Hamilton: George Russell crash at Qatar GP '100 per cent my fault' as he apologises to Mercedes |url=https://www.skysports.com/f1/news/12433/12980613/lewis-hamilton-george-russell-collision-100-per-cent-my-fault-as-he-apologises-to-mercedes-at-qatar-gp |accessdate=12 November 2023 |website=skysports.com}}</ref>

Russell salvaged a measure of pride with a third-place finish at the {{F1 GP|2023|Abu Dhabi}}, which clinched second place in the Constructors' Championship for Mercedes. He finished eighth in the Drivers' Championship, the lowest for a Mercedes driver since {{F1|2012}}, and 59 points behind Hamilton. After the Abu Dhabi race, Russell commented that he had "let the side down a couple of times this year", but that it meant "a huge amount" to help the team finish second.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.russell-delighted-to-seal-p2-in-constructors-for-mercedes-as-abu-dhabi.1aob76YCwfrGMLnv5CWUb1.html |title=Russell delighted to seal P2 in constructors' for Mercedes as Abu Dhabi podium concludes 'challenging season' |website=formula1.com |date=26 November 2023 |accessdate=26 November 2023}}</ref> Although he called his own season "a complete disaster",<ref name=":5" /> Mercedes gave him a two-year contract extension.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.mercedesamgf1.com/news/mercedes-extends-driver-line-up-through-2025 |title=Mercedes Extends Driver Line-Up Through 2025 |website=mercedesamgf1.com |date=31 August 2023 |accessdate=1 September 2023}}</ref>

====2024: Final year with Hamilton====
[[File:FIA F1 Austria 2024 Nr. 63 Russell.jpg|thumb|left|Russell at the [[2024 Austrian Grand Prix]], where he took his second career win.]]
For the [[2024 Formula One World Championship|2024 season]], Mercedes fundamentally changed its design concept.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Wood |first=Will |date=4 May 2024 |title=Mercedes swapped one extreme for another with 2024 car design - Russell |url=https://www.racefans.net/2024/05/05/mercedes-swapped-one-extreme-for-another-with-2024-car-design-russell/ |access-date=9 December 2024 |website=RaceFans}}</ref> The new [[Mercedes W15]] was fast but inconsistent, hard on tyres, and difficult to set up properly.<ref name=":02">{{Cite web |last=Hughes |first=Mark |date=24 November 2024 |title=F1 king of cool: why George Russell always had winning hand in Vegas |url=https://www.motorsportmagazine.com/articles/single-seaters/f1/f1-king-of-cool-why-george-russell-always-had-winning-hand-in-vegas/ |access-date=25 November 2024 |website=Motor Sport Magazine}}</ref> Although the team was not competitive until midseason, Russell commented that the staff was "making progress" behind the scenes.<ref>{{cite web |date=20 May 2024 |title=Russell won't 'sulk' over losing position to Hamilton in Emilia-Romagna Grand Prix after 'lonely race' for Mercedes |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/russell-wont-sulk-over-losing-position-to-hamilton-in-emilia-romagna-grand.2pMtQP5RZRr64Kb2lg4UtN |accessdate=29 July 2024 |website=formula1.com}}</ref> At round three, the {{F1 GP|2024|Australian}}, Russell crashed heavily while trying to overtake Fernando Alonso (who received a 20-second penalty for brake-checking Russell) for sixth place on the penultimate lap.<ref>{{Cite news |last1=Slater |first1=Luke |last2=Cary |first2=Tom |date=24 March 2024 |title=George Russell's safety fears after horror crash at Australian GP |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/formula-1/2024/03/24/australian-grand-prix-2024-live-updates-latest-melbourne/ |access-date=5 March 2025 |work=The Telegraph |language=en-GB |issn=0307-1235}}</ref> The accident left him immobile and defenceless behind a 250 km/h blind turn for ten seconds before the race director deployed the virtual safety car. However, he emerged unscathed and met with Alonso to smooth things over. Following the race, he called for automated safety cars to prevent similar incidents.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Wade |first=Stephen |date=4 April 2024 |title=Russell was 'waiting for a disaster to happen' after he crashed at the Australian GP |url=https://www.sandiegouniontribune.com/2024/04/04/russell-was-waiting-for-a-disaster-to-happen-after-he-crashed-at-the-australian-gp/ |access-date=5 March 2025 |website=San Diego Union-Tribune |language=en-US}}</ref>

Come the midseason, Mercedes scored podium finishes in six consecutive races. Russell reeled off some of his best results in years, including a pole and podium in [[2024 Canadian Grand Prix|Montreal]],<ref>{{Cite web |date=8 June 2024 |title='I've missed this feeling!' – Russell hails Mercedes progress after Canada pole as he vows to 'go for it' on race day |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/ive-missed-this-feeling-russell-hails-mercedes-progress-after-canada-pole-as.3FNoF51rSbAhHwUKUjTn2u |access-date=9 June 2024 |website=Formula 1® - The Official F1® Website}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |date=9 June 2024 |title=Verstappen beats Norris to victory in thrilling wet/dry Canadian GP |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/verstappen-beats-norris-to-victory-in-thrilling-wet-dry-canadian-gp.6ytkbh7iDTWC3pJBwiaboI |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240609235243/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/verstappen-beats-norris-to-victory-in-thrilling-wet-dry-canadian-gp.6ytkbh7iDTWC3pJBwiaboI |archive-date=9 June 2024 |access-date=10 June 2024 |website=Formula1.com}}</ref> his second career race victory at [[2024 Austrian Grand Prix|Spielberg]] (albeit after the first two drivers collided in front of him),<ref>{{cite news |date=30 June 2024 |title=Russell claims surprise win in Austria after Verstappen and Norris dramatically collide in battle for the lead |website=Formula1.com |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/russell-claims-surprise-win-in-austria-after-verstappen-and-norris.2Kmxvn4a42JYDFhvklagYk|access-date=30 June 2024}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.skysports.com/f1/news/12433/13161229/austrian-gp-george-russell-ends-mercedes-win-drought-after-max-verstappen-lando-norris-collision|title=Austrian GP: George Russell ends Mercedes win drought after Max Verstappen-Lando Norris collision|website=skysports.com|first=James|last=Galloway|date=1 July 2024|accessdate=29 July 2024}}</ref> a pole at [[2024 British Grand Prix|Silverstone]] (followed by a mechanical retirement),<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/hamilton-beats-verstappen-to-first-win-since-2021-with-record-breaking-9th.3teU9bznaWJlC2TGAYh0Vl|title=Hamilton beats Verstappen to first win since 2021 with record-breaking 9th British Grand Prix victory|website=formula1.com|date=7 July 2024|accessdate=29 July 2024}}</ref> and the first Formula One race win (at [[2024 Belgian Grand Prix|Spa]]) lost to a post-race disqualification since [[1994 Belgian Grand Prix|1994]],<ref name=":20" /><ref>{{cite news |date=28 July 2024 |title=Russell takes incredible victory in Belgium on aging tyres after thrilling late-race chase from Hamilton |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/russell-takes-incredible-victory-in-belgium-on-aging-tyres-after-thrilling.3FufXdo4r40I7kv5mJLMMR |access-date=28 July 2024 |website=Formula1.com}}</ref> for which the team took responsibility.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/wolff-apologises-to-russell-after-mercedes-mistake-leads-to-belgian-gp.3iQ5OuQj81l7DQbCaYKKt9|title=Wolff apologises to Russell after Mercedes 'mistake' leads to Belgian GP disqualification|website=formula1.com|date=28 July 2024|accessdate=29 July 2024}}</ref> However, the media opined that he could have won the Canadian Grand Prix.<ref name=":14" />

The team's form became more inconsistent as the year went on, but Russell challenged for wins at several races. At the {{F1GP|2024|São Paulo}}, Russell was leading the race until Mercedes ordered him to pit for new tyres right before a red-flag gave his competitors a free tyre change.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Powling |first=Taylor |date=10 November 2024 |title=Mercedes explains call to overrule George Russell in F1 Brazil GP |url=https://www.motorsportweek.com/2024/11/10/mercedes-explains-call-to-overrule-george-russell-in-f1-brazil-gp/ |access-date=11 November 2024 |website=Motorsport Week}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Mann-Bryans |first=Mark |date=3 November 2024 |title=Frustrated Russell wanted to ignore Mercedes pit call in Brazilian GP |url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/frustrated-russell-wanted-to-ignore-mercedes-pit-call-in-brazilian-gp/10670393/ |access-date=4 November 2024 |website=www.motorsport.com}}</ref> Russell dominated the {{F1GP|2024|Las Vegas}}, qualifying on pole and leading 49 of 50 laps to take his third career victory.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/f1-las-vegas-gp-russell-wins-verstappen-fourth-title/10675984/|title=F1 Las Vegas GP: Verstappen secures fourth title as Russell dominates race|date=24 November 2024|access-date=24 November 2024|website=[[Autosport]]|first=Jake|last=Boxall-Legge}}</ref> Russell again qualified on pole in [[2024 Qatar Grand Prix|Qatar]] after [[Max Verstappen]] was handed a grid penalty for driving unnecessarily slowly ahead of Russell, who was on an out-lap.<ref>{{cite web |last=Benson |first=Andrew |date=30 November 2024 |title=Russell promoted to pole by Verstappen grid penalty |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/articles/cy7d7mn83e5o |access-date=2 December 2024 |website=[[BBC Sport]]}}</ref> Verstappen condemned Russell's appeals to the stewards for his penalty, stating he "lost all respect" for him,<ref>{{cite web |last=Benson |first=Andrew |date=1 December 2024 |title=Verstappen has 'lost all respect' for Russell |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/articles/c0rnwzvd9y9o |access-date=2 December 2024 |website=[[BBC Sport]]}}</ref> and warned Russell that he would overtake him at any cost<ref>{{Cite web |last1=Boxall-Legge |first1=Jake |last2=Kalinauckas |first2=Alex |date=1 December 2024 |title=Verstappen 'lost all respect' for Russell after Qatar GP stewards' room conduct |url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/verstappen-lost-all-respect-for-russell-after-qatar-gp-stewards-room-conduct/10678443/ |access-date=2 December 2024 |website=Motorsport.com}}</ref>—Russell claimed he said he would 'put him in the wall', which Verstappen denied.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/articles/cn4x21xwp8go |title=I'm not going to take Verstappen attacks - Russell |website=[[BBC Sport]] |date=5 December 2024 |access-date=5 December 2024 |first=Andrew |last=Benson}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last1=Sutill |first1=Josh |last2=Straw |first2=Edd |last3=Hughes |first3=Mark |date=5 December 2024 |title='Put you on your f***ing head' - Verstappen-Russell row escalates |url=https://www.the-race.com/formula-1/put-you-on-your-f-ing-head-extraordinary-verstappen-russell-f1-row-escalation/ |access-date=5 December 2024 |website=The Race}}</ref> Verstappen overtook him into turn one, with Russell finishing fourth after two safety car periods.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/articles/cgrwj08xgv9o |website=[[BBC Sport]] |first=Andrew |last=Benson |date=1 December 2024| access-date=2 December 2024 |title=Verstappen wins in Qatar after Norris penalty}}</ref>

Russell finished sixth in the Drivers' Championship, 22 points ahead of Hamilton.<ref>{{Cite web |title=2024 Driver Standings |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/results/2024/drivers |access-date=9 December 2024 |website=Formula 1® - The Official F1® Website}}</ref> The team fell from second place to fourth in the Constructors' Championship, but scored four wins,<ref>{{Cite web |date=24 February 2025 |title=Wolff launches 2025 Mercedes: 'Exciting new era' |url=https://www.espn.com/f1/story/_/id/43993158/mercedes-rolls-2025-formula-1-car-bahrain |access-date=27 October 2025 |website=ESPN.com |language=en}}</ref> quadrupling its total from the prior two seasons.<ref name=":0" />

During the three years of the Russell-Hamilton partnership, the Mercedes drivers were evenly matched on track.<ref>{{Cite web |date=8 December 2024 |title=Our verdict on the end of Hamilton-Mercedes + what it means for 2025 |url=https://www.the-race.com/formula-1/our-verdict-lewis-hamilton-end-to-mercedes-stint/ |access-date=9 December 2024 |website=The Race}}</ref> Russell outscored Hamilton in two out of three seasons, recorded three wins to Hamilton's two, and outqualified Hamilton 39–29,<ref>{{Cite web |last=Benson |first=Andrew |date=6 March 2025 |title=George Russell on partnering Lewis Hamilton, Max Verstappen and how he believes 'my time will come' |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/formula1/articles/cvge7048ppdo |access-date=24 March 2025 |website=BBC Sport |language=en-GB}}</ref> while Hamilton scored 20 podiums to Russell's 14<ref>{{Cite web |last=Gassman |first=Alex |date=4 December 2024 |title=Lewis Hamilton and George Russell tied on points after 3 years as Mercedes teammates |url=https://oversteer48.com/hamilton-russell-tied-points/ |access-date=9 December 2024 |website=oversteer48}}</ref> and beat Russell on total points (697–695) after overtaking Russell on the final lap of his [[2024 Abu Dhabi Grand Prix|final race with Mercedes]].<ref name=":16">{{Cite web |last=Benson |first=Andrew |date=8 December 2024 |title=Lewis Hamilton says he 'finished on a high' at Mercedes after 12 years together |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/formula1/articles/cq8qkkzq2lgo |access-date=9 December 2024 |website=BBC Sport}}</ref> After the 2024 season ended, Russell said that he "learned so much from [Hamilton] as a driver and a person,"<ref name=":16" /> and wrote on his personal website that Hamilton "is not only the greatest driver of all time," but also "the type of person that every racing driver should aspire to be."<ref>{{Cite web |date=8 December 2024 |title=Fifth-place finish for George in season finale |url=https://www.georgerussell63.com/press/fifth-place-finish-for-george-in-season-finale |access-date=9 December 2024 |website=GeorgeRussell63.com}}</ref>

====2025: Contract year====
[[File:2025 Japan GP - Mercedes - George Russell - FP2.jpg|thumb|right|Russell (pictured at the {{F1GP|2025|Japanese}}) was partnered by rookie [[Andrea Kimi Antonelli]] in {{F1|2025}}.|alt=Russell driving the Mercedes W16 at the 2025 Japanese Grand Prix]]
In {{F1|2025}}, Russell faced a [[Contract year phenomenon|contract year]].<ref name=":33">{{Cite web |last=Kisby |first=Cambridge |date=12 February 2025 |title=Every F1 driver out of contract at the end of 2025 |url=https://www.motorsportmagazine.com/articles/single-seaters/f1/every-f1-driver-out-of-contract-at-the-end-of-2025/ |access-date=5 March 2025 |website=Motor Sport Magazine |language=en-GB}}</ref> He also received a new teammate, eighteen-year-old academy driver [[Kimi Antonelli]], who was hyped as "F1's next big thing."<ref>{{Cite web |last=Edmondson |first=Laurence |date=15 October 2024 |title=Heir to Hamilton's throne: Antonelli is F1's next big thing |url=https://www.espn.com/racing/f1/story/_/id/41810178/heir-lewis-hamilton-throne-andrea-kimi-antonelli-f1-mercedes-next-big-thing |access-date=27 October 2025 |website=ESPN.com |language=en}}</ref> Defending World Constructors' Champions [[McLaren]] were heavily favoured to claim both titles, and did. At the start of the season, Russell opined that the [[McLaren MCL39|MCL39]] was fast enough to win every Grand Prix.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Benson |first=Andrew |date=20 March 2025 |title=Chinese Grand Prix: McLaren advantage bigger than Red Bull ever had, says George Russell |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/formula1/articles/c62z1nyw7g4o |access-date=23 March 2025 |website=BBC Sport |language=en-GB}}</ref> McLaren dismissed Russell's prediction as hyperbolic,<ref>{{Cite news |last=Cary |first=Tom |date=21 March 2025 |title=Lando Norris accuses British rival George Russell of 'playing mind games' |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/formula-1/2025/03/21/lando-norris-accuses-george-russell-mind-games/ |access-date=23 March 2025 |work=The Telegraph |language=en-GB |issn=0307-1235}}</ref> but it proceeded to dominate the constructors' race with seven 1–2 finishes and 12 wins in the first 18 races.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Saunders |first=Nate |date=5 October 2025 |title=McLaren win back-to-back F1 constructors' championship; 10th overall |url=https://www.espn.com/f1/story/_/id/46332070/mclaren-wins-back-back-f1-constructors-title |access-date=5 October 2025 |website=ESPN.com |language=en}}</ref> In addition, McLaren's [[Lando Norris]] was crowned Drivers' Champion at the [[2025 Abu Dhabi Grand Prix|final race of the season]].<ref name=":50" /> 

Russell opened the season with four podiums in six races at [[2025 Australian Grand Prix|Albert Park]], [[2025 Chinese Grand Prix|Shanghai]], [[2025 Bahrain Grand Prix|Sakhir]], and [[2025 Miami Grand Prix|Miami]], predominantly trailing one or both McLarens.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Coleman |first=Madeline |date=17 March 2025 |title=In Kimi Antonelli's F1 debut, Mercedes glimpses a hopeful post-Hamilton future |url=https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/6208349/2025/03/17/kimi-antonelli-mercedes-f1-australian-gp/ |access-date=18 March 2025 |work=The New York Times |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331}}</ref><ref name=":39">{{Cite web |last=Mann-Bryans |first=Mark |date=23 March 2025 |title=F1 Chinese GP: Piastri dominates, Norris defies brake woes to complete McLaren 1-2 |url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/f1-chinese-gp-piastri-wins-in-dominant-mclaren-1-2/10706307/ |access-date=23 March 2025 |website=[[Autosport]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |language=en}}</ref><ref name=":40">{{Cite web |date=13 April 2025 |title=Bahrain GP: Oscar Piastri claims dominant win as George Russell holds off Lando Norris for second |url=https://www.skysports.com/f1/news/12433/13347935/bahrain-gp-oscar-piastri-claims-dominant-win-as-george-russell-holds-off-lando-norris-for-second |access-date=13 April 2025 |website=Sky Sports |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Heverin |first=Dane |date=4 May 2025 |title=Piastri nails historic title statement as Norris dealt fresh blow in Miami drama |url=https://www.foxsports.com.au/motorsport/f1-2025-miami-grand-prix-race-live-updates-oscar-piastri-grid-position-start-time-aest-starting-grid-result-how-to-stream/news-story/f5e94b0a0c02c40b0899c7f18c706b8a |access-date=4 May 2025 |website=Fox Sports |language=en}}</ref> In Australia, he raced conservatively in intermittently rainy conditions and inherited third place when [[Oscar Piastri]] went off track.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Harrington |first=Alex |date=16 March 2025 |title=George Russell's strategy gamble pays off in rain-hit Australia GP: &quot;Most decisive decision I've ever taken&quot; |url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/george-russells-strategy-gamble-pays-off-in-rain-hit-australia-gp-most-decisive-decision-ive-ever-t/10704037/ |access-date=16 March 2025 |website=[[Motorsport.com]] |language=en}}</ref><ref name=":38">{{Cite web |date=16 March 2025 |title=Russell podium pride as Mercedes 'a step ahead of Ferrari' |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/russell-believes-mercedes-look-a-step-ahead-of-ferrari-as-he-shares-podium.2SzY70eXKOspW2fudHWMmh |access-date=16 March 2025 |website=Formula 1® - The Official F1® Website |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=16 March 2025 |title=Home race 'curse' knocks Piastri off podium |url=https://www.espn.com/f1/story/_/id/44273640/australian-gp-podium-slips-away-oscar-piastri-suffers-home-race-curse |access-date=16 March 2025 |website=ESPN.com |language=en}}</ref> At Shanghai, Russell qualified second for the main race, splitting the two McLarens; strong teamwork from McLaren allowed Lando Norris to pass him at turn one,<ref>{{Cite web |last=Thukral |first=Rachit |date=23 March 2025 |title=George Russell: I would have passed Lando Norris if I had half a lap more |url=https://www.crash.net/f1/news/1065809/1/george-russell-i-would-have-passed-lando-norris-if-i-had-half-lap-more |access-date=23 March 2025 |website=Crash.net |language=en}}</ref> and Russell finished third.<ref name=":39" /> After an uneventful fifth-place finish at [[2025 Japanese Grand Prix|Suzuka]] with almost no overtaking within the top 10,<ref>{{Cite news |last1=Harrington |first1=Alex |last2=Vording |first2=Ronald |date=7 April 2025 |title=Max Verstappen Explains Lack of Overtaking After 'Dull' Japanese GP |url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/max-verstappen-explains-lack-of-overtaking-after-dull-japanese-gp/10710845/ |access-date=13 April 2025 |work=[[Motorsport.com]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Chiu |first=Nigel |date=6 April 2025 |title=Japanese GP: Max Verstappen fends off Lando Norris and Oscar Piastri to win his first F1 race of 2025 season |url=https://www.skysports.com/f1/news/12433/13342479/japanese-gp-max-verstappen-fends-off-lando-norris-and-oscar-piastri-to-win-his-first-f1-race-of-2025-season |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250407105511/https://www.skysports.com/f1/news/12433/13342479/japanese-gp-max-verstappen-fends-off-lando-norris-and-oscar-piastri-to-win-his-first-f1-race-of-2025-season |archive-date=7 April 2025 |access-date=13 April 2025 |work=Sky Sports |language=en-GB |url-status=live }}</ref> Russell bounced back in Bahrain: he fended off Norris in the closing laps to finish second—overcoming faulty brakes and electronics<ref>{{Cite web |last=Mee |first=Lydia |date=13 April 2025 |title=FIA delivers verdict after George Russell's DRS issue scrutinised |url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/fia-delivers-verdict-after-george-russells-drs-issue-scrutinised/10713017/ |access-date=13 April 2025 |website=[[Motorsport.com]] |language=en}}</ref>—and received widespread praise from the racing press for his adaptive performance.{{Efn|Per several sources:<ref>{{Cite news |last=Coleman |first=Madeline |date=14 April 2025 |title=How George Russell finished second in Bahrain Grand Prix with malfunctioning car |url=https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/6276529/2025/04/14/george-russell-bahrain-grand-prix-mercedes-f1/ |access-date=14 April 2025 |work=The New York Times |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Chinchero |first=Roberto |date=14 April 2025 |title=Russell moves closer to new Mercedes F1 contract |url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/russell-moves-closer-to-new-mercedes-f1-contract/10713402/ |access-date=14 April 2025 |website=Autosport |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last1=Mitchell-Malm |first1=Scott |last2=Straw |first2=Edd |last3=Noble |first3=Jon |date=14 April 2025 |title=Everything we learned at F1's Bahrain Grand Prix |url=https://www.the-race.com/formula-1/everything-we-learned-2025-f1-bahrain-grand-prix/ |access-date=14 April 2025 |website=The Race |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Hughes |first=Mark |date=14 April 2025 |title=Monday Morning Debrief: How George Russell held onto a brilliant P2 in Bahrain – despite car failures, tyre woes and a charging Lando Norris on his tail |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/monday-morning-debrief-how-russell-held-onto-a-brilliant-p2-in-bahrain.DLYkcuH5nFYLyQxogtNQe |access-date=14 April 2025 |website=Formula One |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Richards |first=Giles |date=13 April 2025 |title=McLaren's Oscar Piastri surges to dominant victory at Bahrain F1 GP |url=https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2025/apr/13/mclarens-oscar-piastri-surges-to-dominant-victory-at-bahrain-f1-gp |access-date=14 April 2025 |work=The Guardian |language=en-GB |issn=0261-3077}}</ref>}} Struggling with tyre overheating, Mercedes laboured to fifth- and sixth-place finishes in [[2025 Saudi Arabian Grand Prix|Jeddah]].<ref>{{Cite news |last=Selleck |first=Emily |date=20 April 2025 |title=Wolff laments "worst performance of the season" for Mercedes in Jeddah |url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/wolff-laments-worst-performance-of-the-season-for-mercedes-in-jeddah/10715585/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250428134159/https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/wolff-laments-worst-performance-of-the-season-for-mercedes-in-jeddah/10715585/ |archive-date=28 April 2025 |access-date=4 May 2025 |work=Autosport |language=en |url-status=live }}</ref> At Miami, Russell was out-qualified by Antonelli for the first time,<ref>{{Cite web |last=Chiu |first=Nigel |date=4 May 2025 |title=Miami Grand Prix: Will rain spoil Lando Norris' bid to beat Max Verstappen and take championship lead from Oscar Piastri? |url=https://www.skysports.com/f1/news/12433/13360605/miami-grand-prix-will-rain-spoil-lando-norris-bid-to-beat-max-verstappen-and-take-championship-lead-from-oscar-piastri |access-date=4 May 2025 |website=Sky Sports |language=en}}</ref> before an unconventional decision to start the Grand Prix on hard tyres was rewarded with a near-free [[pit stop]] under [[virtual safety car]] conditions, helping him finish third.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Khorounzhiy |first=Valentin |date=4 May 2025 |title=McLaren destroys F1 rivals in Miami GP as Piastri wins again |url=https://www.the-race.com/formula-1/mclaren-destroys-f1-rivals-in-miami-gp-as-oscar-piastri-wins-again/ |access-date=4 May 2025 |website=The Race |language=en}}</ref>

Mercedes began testing major upgrades during the Imola-Monaco-Barcelona tripleheader,<ref>{{Cite web |last1=Mitchell-Malm |first1=Scott |last2=Noble |first2=Jon |date=16 May 2025 |title=Mercedes' first big update of 2025 revealed |url=https://www.the-race.com/formula-1/mercedes-imola-f1-package-after-lacking-enormous-or-sexy-upgrades/ |access-date=19 May 2025 |website=The Race |language=en}}</ref> but the team generally lacked the pace to compete for wins. The [[Mercedes W16]]'s new suspension was particularly enigmatic: introduced at Imola, it was withdrawn after one middling race. The team reintroduced it at Montreal three rounds later,<ref>{{Cite web |last=Noble |first=Jon |date=12 June 2025 |title=Mercedes reverts to new suspension it parked after its debut |url=https://www.the-race.com/formula-1/mercedes-reverts-to-new-suspension-it-parked-after-its-debut/ |access-date=5 August 2025 |website=The Race |language=en}}</ref> and Russell controlled the race from start to finish, picking up his maiden Formula One [[Hat-trick (Formula One)|hat-trick]] (taking pole, winning, and setting the fastest lap).<ref>{{Cite web |date=15 June 2025 |title=Russell wins in Montreal as Mercedes rule the roost |url=https://press.pirelli.com/russell-wins-in-montreal-as-mercedes-rule-the-roost/ |access-date=17 June 2025 |website=Pirelli |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=16 June 2025 |title=Antonelli: F1 podium 'better than I imagined' |url=https://www.espn.com/f1/story/_/id/45520301/antonelli-f1-podium-better-imagined |access-date=17 June 2025 |website=ESPN.com |language=en}}</ref> However, the improvement quickly faded, and at [[2025 Belgian Grand Prix|Spa-Francorchamps]], Russell noted that the temperamental W16 was struggling even in relatively favourable conditions.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Mee |first=Lydia |date=27 July 2025 |title=George Russell to hold &quot;big meeting&quot; with Mercedes over F1 performance drop |url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/george-russell-to-hold-big-meeting-with-mercedes-over-f1-performance-drop/10745965/ |access-date=28 July 2025 |website=[[Motorsport.com]] |language=en}}</ref> Mercedes reverted to the older suspension at [[2025 Hungarian Grand Prix|Hungary]] one round later,<ref>{{Cite web |last1=Suttill |first1=Josh |last2=Straw |first2=Edd |date=31 July 2025 |title=Mercedes makes another spec U-turn to stop F1 form tailspin |url=https://www.the-race.com/formula-1/mercedes-rear-suspension-upgrade-dropped-second-time-russell-antonelli/ |access-date=5 August 2025 |website=The Race |language=en}}</ref> and Russell scored a podium after hunting down [[Charles Leclerc]], whose car was dramatically fading.<ref>{{Cite news |last1=Smith |first1=Luke |last2=Coleman |first2=Madeline |date=3 August 2025 |title=Hungarian Grand Prix: Norris wins a thriller over Piastri, Leclerc's victory evaporates |url=https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/6533166/2025/08/03/hungarian-grand-prix-2025-result-lando-norris-mclaren-charles-leclerc/ |access-date=5 August 2025 |work=The New York Times |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331}}</ref> Aside from those two podiums, Russell's next-best finish was a chaotic fourth-place at [[2025 Spanish Grand Prix|Barcelona]] where he qualified fourth, lost two places at the start, undercut [[Lewis Hamilton]], passed fourth-placed [[Max Verstappen]] in the closing laps after a safety car restart, and was hit by Verstappen on track near the end of the race, for which the Dutchman expressed regret.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Cary |first=Tom |date=1 June 2025 |title=George Russell: Disqualify Max Verstappen for 'deliberate' crash |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/formula-1/2025/06/01/max-verstappen-vs-george-russell-crash-breakdown/ |access-date=1 June 2025 |work=The Telegraph |language=en-GB |issn=0307-1235}}</ref>{{efn|After tussling with Russell and Charles Leclerc, Verstappen was asked to give back fourth place to Russell, which proved to be a strategy error on Red Bull's part. An infuriated Verstappen slowed down before bumping wheels with Russell (he ultimately gave up the place and received a ten-second penalty). Verstappen said that his move was "not right and shouldn't have happened", but claimed it was a "misjudgment";<ref>{{Cite web |last=Noble |first=Jon |date=2 June 2025 |title=Verstappen concedes Russell clash shouldn't have happened |url=https://www.the-race.com/formula-1/verstappen-says-russell-f1-spanish-gp-clash-should-not-happen/ |access-date=2 June 2025 |website=The Race |language=en}}</ref> several commentators thought it was intentional.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Mee |first=Lydia |date=1 June 2025 |title=Rosberg questions Max Verstappen's "lenient" Spanish GP penalty: "That's a black flag" |url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/rosberg-questions-max-verstappens-lenient-spanish-gp-penalty-thats-a-black-flag/10728782/ |access-date=1 June 2025 |website=[[Motorsport.com]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Hughes |first=Mark |date=2 June 2025 |title=Mark Hughes: Needless F1 team order enraged already-beaten Verstappen |url=https://www.motorsportmagazine.com/articles/single-seaters/f1/mark-hughes-enraged-verstappen-was-already-beaten-before-needless-team-order/ |access-date=2 June 2025 |website=Motor Sport Magazine |language=en-GB}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=2 June 2025 |title=Should Verstappen have been disqualified from the Spanish GP? Our writers have their say |url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/should-verstappen-have-been-disqualified-from-the-spanish-gp-our-writers-have-their-say/10728883/?fbclid=IwY2xjawKqlhJleHRuA2FlbQIxMQBicmlkETFOMzRzWk52RGF1aWVYcENXAR6ZnsqynhgKyCpP8KbI1O2c4NRDSrAv8Cp5T3kRcMea3aiX0SxXYUpPNeajIQ_aem_X7nF8SB3Rm0A-hVdPIKO7Q |access-date=2 June 2025 |website=www.autosport.com |language=en}}</ref>}} Verstappen received a time penalty for hitting Russell, which cost him nine championship points. Ironically, after a late-season charge, Verstappen closed most of the gap to Lando Norris in the Drivers' Championship, but lost the title by two points.<ref name=":50">{{Cite news |last=Cary |first=Tom |date=2025-12-07 |title=Max Verstappen bristles at suggestion George Russell crash cost him the title |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/formula-1/2025/12/07/max-verstappen-george-russell-crash-f1-title/ |access-date=2025-12-08 |work=The Telegraph |language=en-GB |issn=0307-1235}}</ref>

Following the summer break, Russell finished fifth at [[2025 Italian Grand Prix|Monza]].<ref>{{Cite news |last1=Smith |first1=Luke |last2=Coleman |first2=Madeline |date=7 September 2025 |title=Italian GP: Verstappen sets new F1 record as McLaren orders spark late drama |url=https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/6607857/2025/09/07/f1-italian-gp-recap-max-verstappen-win-oscar-piastri-lando-norris/ |access-date=21 September 2025 |work=The New York Times |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331}}</ref> He then scored his seventh podium of the season at [[2025 Azerbaijan Grand Prix|Baku]] with a second-place finish, having struggled with a respiratory illness all weekend.<ref>{{Cite web |last1=Bailey |first1=Michael |last2=Smith |first2=Luke |date=21 September 2025 |title=How Max Verstappen won F1's 2025 Azerbaijan Grand Prix after Oscar Piastri's Lap 1 crash |url=https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/live-blogs/f1-azerbaijan-gp-live-updates-race-times-results/KgUScRQtq1Tp/ |access-date=21 September 2025 |website=The Athletic |language=en-US}}</ref> The next round at [[2025 Singapore Grand Prix|Singapore]], Russell surprised commentators by taking pole by 0.182 seconds on a track where Mercedes was not expected to be competitive.<ref name=":46">{{Cite web |last=Hughes |first=Mark |date=5 October 2025 |title=What sank Verstappen and Norris's Singapore GP win chances |url=https://www.the-race.com/formula-1/max-verstappen-neutralised-george-russell-biggest-threat/ |access-date=5 October 2025 |website=The Race |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Benson |first=Andrew |date=4 October 2025 |title=Russell claims stunning Singapore pole |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/formula1/articles/cqlzxdr01yeo |access-date=5 October 2025 |website=BBC Sport |language=en-GB}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Cozens |first=Jack |date=4 October 2025 |title=Russell takes shock Mercedes pole at Singapore GP |url=https://www.the-race.com/formula-1/russell-takes-singapore-gp-pole-verstappen-angered-by-norris/ |access-date=5 October 2025 |website=The Race |language=en}}</ref> After Verstappen (who started second) unsuccessfully gambled on used soft tyres at the start, Russell got out to a large lead and cruised to victory.<ref name=":46" /> After the win, Mercedes announced that Russell had re-signed for the 2026 season;<ref name=":49" /> it later extended the deal to 2027.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Cary |first=Tom |date=26 October 2025 |title=What happened when I played padel with George Russell |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/formula-1/2025/10/26/george-russell-interview-verstappen-padel-mercedes-2026-f1/ |access-date=26 October 2025 |work=The Telegraph |language=en-GB |issn=0307-1235}}</ref><ref name=":54">{{Cite news |last=Chinchero |first=Roberto |date=4 July 2026 |title=George Russell and Lewis Hamilton contract renewals reveal the Max Verstappen-McLaren rumours to be nonsense |url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/george-russell-and-lewis-hamilton-contract-renewals-reveal-the-max-verstappen-mclaren-rumours-to-be/10836161/ |access-date=5 July 2026 |work=[[Motorsport.com]] |language=en|last2=Codling|first2=Stuart}}</ref> The team reportedly raised his salary to £30m/year, making him the third-highest-paid driver in Formula One after Verstappen and Hamilton.<ref name=":49">{{Cite web |last=Jackson |first=Kieran |date=15 October 2025 |title=Inside Russell's new Mercedes deal – and why Brit is now poised for F1 title charge |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/f1/george-russell-f1-mercedes-contract-salary-antonelli-b2845889.html |access-date=21 October 2025 |website=The Independent |language=en}}</ref> The team's focus shifted to 2026,<ref>{{Cite web |last1=Vinel |first1=Ben |last2=Faturos |first2=Federico |date=2025-12-07 |title="Overtakes in obscure locations" predicted for F1 2026 with post-DRS cars |url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/overtakes-in-obscure-locations-predicted-for-f1-2026-with-post-drs-cars/10774342/ |access-date=2025-12-08 |website=[[Motorsport.com]] |language=en}}</ref> and Russell scored one podium in the final six races, at [[2025 Las Vegas Grand Prix|Las Vegas]], where he dealt with steering and tyre issues. It was his career-best ninth podium of the season.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Curtis |first=Charles |title=Why McLaren was disqualified from F1 Las Vegas Grand Prix |url=https://ftw.usatoday.com/story/sports/2025/11/23/mclaren-disqualified-f1-las-vegas-grand-prix/87432493007/ |access-date=2025-11-23 |website=For The Win |language=en-US}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=2025-11-23 |title=George Russell explains dramatic late-race pace concern |url=https://racingnews365.com/george-russell-explains-dramatic-late-race-pace-concern |access-date=2025-11-23 |website=RacingNews365 |language=en}}</ref>

Russell finished fourth in the Drivers' Championship with 319 points, 169 ahead of Antonelli.<ref>{{Cite web |title=2025 Drivers' Standings |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/results/2025/drivers |access-date=2025-12-08 |website=Formula 1® - The Official F1® Website |language=en}}</ref> Mercedes returned to second in the Drivers' Championship.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Galloway |first=James |date=2025-12-07 |title=Lando Norris wins Formula 1 world title for first time in Abu Dhabi GP decider to pip Max Verstappen to 2025 crown |url=https://www.skysports.com/f1/news/12040/13480428/lando-norris-wins-formula-1-world-title-for-first-time-in-abu-dhabi-gp-decider-to-pip-max-verstappen-to-crown |access-date=2025-12-08 |website=Sky Sports |language=en}}</ref> At the end of the season, ''[[Autosport]]'' ranked Russell the second-best driver in motorsport, between Verstappen and [[Álex Palou]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=2025-12-20 |title=Autosport Top 50 of 2025: #2 George Russell |url=https://www.autosport.com/general/news/autosport-top-50-of-2025-2-george-russell/10785440/ |access-date=2025-12-20 |website=[[Autosport]] |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=2025-12-19 |title=Top 50 Drivers of 2025 |url=https://www.autosport.com/topic/top-50-drivers-of-2025/2805/?brid=1rmfyYYDbBHnezh5ks7Kmw |access-date=2025-12-20 |website=[[Autosport]] |language=en}}</ref> ''[[The Daily Telegraph]]'', ''The Race'', [[The Athletic|''The Athletic'']], and ''Autoevolution'' ranked Russell the second-best driver in Formula One, in each case behind Verstappen and ahead of title-winner Norris.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Slater |first=Luke |date=2025-12-08 |title=F1 driver ratings: Norris misses out on top spot as Hamilton beaten by three rookies |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/formula-1/2025/12/08/driver-ratings-max-verstappen-lewis-hamilton-lando-norris/ |access-date=2025-12-20 |work=The Telegraph |language=en-GB |issn=0307-1235}}</ref><ref name=":51">{{Cite web |date=2025-12-13 |title=Every 2025 F1 driver ranked from worst to best |url=https://www.the-race.com/formula-1/every-2025-f1-driver-ranked-from-worst-to-best/ |access-date=2025-12-20 |website=The Race |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last1=Smith |first1=Luke |last2=Coleman |first2=Madeline |date=2025-12-24 |title=F1's top 10 drivers of 2025: Verstappen shows his rivals 'who's boss' once again |url=https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/6897591/2025/12/24/formula-1-f1-top-10-drivers-2025-verstappen-norris-piastri/ |access-date=2025-12-31 |work=The New York Times |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Spencer |first=Ed |date=2025-12-19 |title=F1: The Class of 2025 End-of-Season Rankings (5–1) |url=https://www.autoevolution.com/news/f1-the-class-of-2025-end-of-season-rankings-51-262908.html |access-date=2025-12-20 |website=autoevolution |language=en}}</ref> In Formula One's official polls, the team principals ranked him fourth and the drivers ranked him third.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Barretto |first=Lawrence |date=2025-12-30 |title=The top 10 drivers of 2025 – as chosen by the drivers |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/exclusive-the-top-10-f1-drivers-of-2025-as-chosen-by-the-drivers.0quz9TQPmSNBITUwz64d9 |access-date=2025-12-31 |website=Formula One |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Barretto |first=Lawrence |date=2025-12-24 |title=The F1 team bosses choose their top 10 drivers of 2025 |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/exclusive-the-f1-team-bosses-choose-their-top-10-drivers-of-2025.30ev5TbzHuK6hnaiv9k7KI |access-date=2025-12-29 |website=Formula One |language=en}}</ref> ''[[Motor Sport (magazine)|Motor Sport]]'' ranked him fifth, although its writers considered slotting him ahead of Norris and Piastri.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2025-12-09 |title=2025 F1 drivers ranked: Who had the best season? |url=https://www.motorsportmagazine.com/articles/single-seaters/f1/2025-f1-drivers-ranked-who-had-the-best-season/ |access-date=2025-12-20 |website=Motor Sport Magazine |language=en-GB}}</ref>

==== 2026: Title contender ====
[[File:2026 Chinese GP - Mercedes - George Russell - Qualifying.jpg|alt=Russell driving the Mercedes W17 at the 2026 Chinese Grand Prix|thumb|Russell driving the [[Mercedes W17|W17]] at the [[2026 Chinese Grand Prix]]]]
Heading into a major regulation change, pundits and bookies predicted that Mercedes would have a strong season.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Smith |first=Luke |date=2026-01-22 |title=Bookies have Mercedes as the F1 2026 favorite. There’s more to it than good past engines |url=https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/6989661/2026/01/22/f1-2026-preseason-favorite-mercedes/ |access-date=2026-03-02 |work=The New York Times |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Straw |first=Edd |last2=Mitchell-Malm |first2=Scott |date=2026-02-22 |title=Ranking the 2026 F1 teams after pre-season testing |url=https://www.the-race.com/formula-1/ranking-the-2026-f1-teams-after-pre-season-testing/ |access-date=2026-03-02 |website=The Race |language=en}}</ref> Russell sought to manage expectations before the season,<ref>{{Cite web |last=Benson |first=Andrew |date=2026-02-02 |title=George Russell 'wants to go head-to-head' with Max Verstappen in 2026 |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/formula1/articles/c1klx1vzxdzo |access-date=2026-03-02 |website=BBC Sport |language=en-GB}}</ref> but at the season-opening {{F1 GP|2026|Australian}}, he took pole three-tenths of a second over teammate Antonelli and eight-tenths of a second over third-placed [[Isack Hadjar]]. ''[[Autosport]]'' called the margin "staggering."<ref>{{Cite web |last=Codling |first=Stuart |date=2026-03-07 |title=How Russell guided his 'go kart' Mercedes to F1 Australian GP pole by a staggering margin |url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/how-russell-guided-his-go-kart-mercedes-to-f1-australian-gp-pole-by-a-staggering-margin/10803079/ |access-date=2026-03-07 |website=[[Autosport]] |language=en}}</ref> He won the race after an extended battle with [[Scuderia Ferrari|Ferrari]]'s [[Charles Leclerc]] in the opening laps. Russell claimed the net lead when Mercedes pitted under [[virtual safety car]] on lap 12 and Ferrari stayed out, gambling for a second safety car later in the race. That gamble failed, so Russell and Antonelli nursed their tyres for 46 laps and cruised to a [[Glossary of motorsport terms#0–9|1–2 finish]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Benson |first=Andrew |date=2026-03-08 |title=Australian Grand Prix result: George Russell wins from Kimi Antonelli as new era F1 era begins |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/formula1/articles/c1l72e7mrn4o |access-date=2026-03-08 |website=BBC Sport |language=en-GB}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Boxall-Legge |first=Jake |date=2026-03-08 |title=Mercedes drew first blood in F1 2026 - but did Ferrari miss a prime opportunity? |url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/mercedes-drew-first-blood-in-f1-2026-but-did-ferrari-miss-a-prime-opportunity/10803456/ |access-date=2026-03-08 |website=[[Autosport]] |language=en}}</ref> With the win, Russell claimed the Drivers' Championship lead for the first time in his career.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.theguardian.com/sport/live/2026/mar/08/australian-grand-prix-f1-melbourne-race-live|title=George Russell wins Australian Grand Prix ahead of Kimi Antonelli|work=[[The Guardian]]|date=8 March 2026|access-date=8 March 2026|last=Richards|first=Giles}}</ref> 

At [[2026 Chinese Grand Prix|Shanghai]], Russell's fortunes began taking a serious turn for the worse, to his teammate Antonelli's benefit. During the sprint race, the Australia pattern repeated, and Russell and Ferrari's [[Lewis Hamilton]] traded the lead six times in the first five laps before Hamilton's tyres faded.<ref>{{Cite web |last= |date=2026-03-14 |title=Chinese Grand Prix: George Russell wins F1 sprint |url=https://www.espn.com/f1/story/_/id/48173287/george-russell-wins-f1-sprint-mercedes-charles-leclerc-lewis-hamilton |access-date=2026-03-14 |website=ESPN.com |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Chinese GP Sprint: George Russell wins for Mercedes after thrilling battle with Lewis Hamilton in Shanghai |url=https://www.skysports.com/f1/news/12433/13519136/chinese-gp-sprint-george-russell-wins-for-mercedes-after-thrilling-battle-with-lewis-hamilton-in-shanghai |access-date=2026-03-14 |website=Sky Sports |language=en}}</ref> However, at the Grand Prix, Russell lost pole to Antonelli after technical issues in qualifying.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Codling |first=Stuart |last2=Vording |first2=Ronald |date=2026-03-15 |title=Mystery problem nearly ruined George Russell's F1 qualifying at Chinese GP |url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/mercedes-yet-to-understand-problem-that-nearly-left-russell-10th-in-china/10805130/ |access-date=2026-03-15 |website=[[Motorsport.com]] |language=en}}</ref> He spent much of the race in traffic with the Ferraris, and finished second, while Antonelli eventually reached clear air and won comfortably.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Chiu |first=Nigel |date=2026-03-15 |title=Chinese GP: Kimi Antonelli claims maiden F1 win from George Russell as Lewis Hamilton gets first Ferrari podium in Shanghai |url=https://www.skysports.com/f1/news/12433/13519942/chinese-gp-kimi-antonelli-claims-maiden-f1-win-from-george-russell-as-lewis-hamilton-gets-first-ferrari-podium-in-shanghai |access-date=2026-03-15 |website=Sky Sports |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Benson |first=Andrew |date=2026-03-15 |title=Chinese Grand Prix 2026: Kimi Antonelli wins ahead of Russell |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/formula1/articles/czx4l44d53eo |access-date=2026-03-15 |website=BBC Sport |language=en-GB}}</ref> Antonelli then seized the championship lead at [[2026 Japanese Grand Prix|Suzuka]], where Russell's race was marred by setup and electronic issues and an ill-timed pit stop.<ref>{{Cite news |date=2026-03-29 |title=George Russell: Mercedes driver says 'one lap of difference' in timing of Japanese GP safety car would have seen him win race |url=https://www.skysports.com/f1/news/12040/13525781/george-russell-mercedes-driver-says-one-lap-of-difference-in-timing-of-japanese-gp-safety-car-would-have-seen-him-win-race |access-date=2026-03-29 |work=Sky Sports}}</ref> At [[2026 Miami Grand Prix|Miami]], Russell beat Antonelli in the sprint, but the Italian beat him on merit in the Grand Prix.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Miami Grand Prix 2026 - F1 Race |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/racing/2026/miami |access-date=2026-05-03 |website=www.formula1.com |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Miami 2026 - Championship • STATS F1 |url=https://www.statsf1.com/en/2026/miami/championnat.aspx |access-date=2026-05-03 |website=www.statsf1.com}}</ref> Russell hoped to bounce back at [[2026 Canadian Grand Prix|Montreal]]. He won the sprint after a race-long duel with Antonelli, and looked to repeat the feat in the Grand Prix, again repeating a duel with his teammate, but retired from the lead with an engine failure.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Benson |first=Andrew |date=2026-05-24 |title=F1 Canadian Grand Prix result: Kimi Antonelli wins as George Russell retires |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/formula1/articles/c9q3d2lglrdo |access-date=2026-06-08 |website=BBC Sport |language=en-GB}}</ref> Now 43 points behind his teammate, things went from bad to worse at [[2026 Monaco Grand Prix|Monaco]], where Russell failed to score at all after a disappointing qualifying, a self-inflicted time penalty, and a team-inflicted [[Drive-through penalty (Formula One)|drive-through penalty]], ultimately finishing in twelfth. Ultimately, the bookmakers' title favourite at the start of the season found himself in third place after the conclusion of the race, 68 points behind Antonelli and two points behind Hamilton.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Benson |first=Andrew |date=2026-06-07 |title=Monaco Grand Prix: Kimi Antonelli and George Russell contrast could hardly be more stark |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/formula1/articles/cd95d3vy34lo |access-date=2026-06-08 |website=BBC Sport |language=en-GB}}</ref> 

Russell began clawing back at [[2026 Barcelona-Catalunya Grand Prix|Barcelona]]. He was the leading driver in two out of three practice sessions and took pole position, but his luck was alternately bad and good: Hamilton seized the lead and won after Russell (again) pitted right before a virtual safety car, and, late into the race, Antonelli passed Russell after Mercedes accidentally changed Russell's race setup during a pit stop. However, Russell still picked up 18 points on Antonelli, who retired with an engine failure.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.skysports.com/f1/news/12433/13553903/barcelona-catalunya-gp-lewis-hamilton-claims-first-grand-prix-win-for-ferrari-as-kimi-antonelli-retires-late-on|title=Barcelona-Catalunya GP: Lewis Hamilton claims first Grand Prix win for Ferrari as Kimi Antonelli retires late on|website=Sky Sports|date=14 June 2026|access-date=14 June 2026}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=D'Alessandro |first=Gianluca |date=2026-06-28 |title=How a Mercedes pit stop error &quot;compromised&quot; George Russell’s Barcelona GP |url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/f1-russell-backstory-mercedes-had-incorrectly-adjusted-the-front-wing-at-the-pit-stop/10830780/ |access-date=2026-06-28 |website=[[Motorsport.com]] |language=en}}</ref> Russell's stars aligned at [[2026 Austrian Grand Prix|Spielberg]]; after running behind Antonelli in two out of three practice sessions, Russell converted his pole position to a dominating second race win of the season; in doing so, he took second in the Drivers' Championship back from Hamilton. Antonelli qualified fourth after misreading the [[Yellow flag (motorsport)|yellow flag]] signal during his final qualifying lap, and was unlucky himself to pit right before a virtual safety car.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Benson |first=Andrew |date=2026-06-28 |title=Austrian Grand Prix: Relief for George Russell as he secures second win of season |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/formula1/articles/c14yr0kpjy1o |access-date=2026-06-28 |website=BBC Sport |language=en-GB}}</ref> [[2026 British Grand Prix|Silverstone]] went similarly to Barcelona: Antonelli beat Russell in the sprint race and was on pace to win the Grand Prix, while Russell's race seemed ruined after a puncture forced yet another pit stop before a virtual safety car. However, Russell finished second, passing Lewis Hamilton by gambling (correctly) that the race would end under safety car conditions. Antonelli initially fell to ninth after part of his car's bodywork broke, and a time penalty dropped him out of the points.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Benson |first=Andrew |date=2026-07-05 |title=British Grand Prix result: Charles Leclerc wins dramatic race from George Russell and Lewis Hamilton |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/formula1/articles/crr8pxxe20zo |access-date=2026-07-05 |website=BBC Sport |language=en-GB}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Benyon |first=Jack |date=2026-07-05 |title=Leclerc wins British GP after bizarre safety car finish |url=https://www.the-race.com/formula-1/british-gp-leclerc-wins-safety-car-finish-f1/ |access-date=2026-07-05 |website=The Race |language=en}}</ref> His fortunes tumbled once more at [[2026 Belgian Grand Prix|Belgium]], where he qualified fourth to Antonelli's pole. During the opening lap of the Grand Prix, he was hit by Hamilton on the run to ''[[Circuit de Spa-Francorchamps|Les Combes]]'', beaching him and forcing him to retire. The contact also inflicted damage to his Mercedes' bodywork.<ref>{{cite news |last=Benson |first=Andrew |title=Belgian Grand Prix result: Kimi Antonelli wins to extend title lead after George Russell crashes out on first lap |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/formula1/articles/cevmymn2kd8o |work=[[BBC Sport]] |date=19 July 2026 |access-date=19 July 2026}}</ref> Having began the weekend 25 points behind Antonelli in the Drivers' Championship, his younger teammate won the Grand Prix to extend his advantage, 50 points ahead; he himself dropped to third behind Hamilton. Following the race, Russell did not put the blame for his retirement on Hamilton, who received a penalty for the incident.<ref>{{cite web |title=Why Hamilton was penalised for Belgian GP clash and why Leclerc was not |url=https://www.the-race.com/formula-1/why-lewis-hamilton-was-penalised-for-belgian-gp-clash-why-charles-leclerc-wasnt/ |website=The Race |date=19 July 2026 |access-date=19 July 2026}}</ref> He stated that the contact was a racing incident and criticised an electrical issue that diminished his engine's power and disallowed battery deployment across ''Eau Rouge'', leaving him vulnerable to other drivers going across the ''Kemmel Straight'',<ref>{{cite web |last=Khorounzhiy |first=Valentin |title=Russell 'going slower than F2 car' before Hamilton incident |url=https://www.the-race.com/formula-1/russell-going-slower-than-f2-car-before-hamilton-incident/ |website=The Race |date=19 July 2026 |access-date=19 July 2026}}</ref> reiterating his criticisms from his team radio message shortly following the incident.<ref>{{cite web |last=Nobel |first=Jonathan |title=What was behind Russell's radio rant - and why it wasn't broadcast live |url=https://www.the-race.com/formula-1/what-was-behind-russells-radio-rant-and-why-it-was-muted/ |website=The Race |date=19 July 2026 |access-date=22 July 2026}}</ref>

==== 2027 ====
Russell and Antonelli are contracted to remain at Mercedes for the [[2027 Formula One season|2027 season]].<ref name=":54" />

== Driver profile ==

=== Driving style ===
In general, Russell favours smooth inputs, car control, and using the entire width of the track to exit a corner.<ref name=":52">{{Cite web |last=Morrison |first=Mac |date=2026-03-05 |title=Exclusive: Mercedes F1 Star George Russell on How You Can Become a Better Driver, Sims, and More |url=https://www.motortrend.com/features/exclusive-interview-mercedes-f1-driver-george-russell |access-date=2026-03-23 |website=MotorTrend |language=en}}</ref> He has specifically been noted for controlling cars that are unstable when entering corners.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Anderson |first=Ben |date=16 December 2022 |title=Which current F1 drivers can drive around a car's problems? |url=https://www.the-race.com/formula-1/which-current-f1-drivers-can-drive-around-a-cars-problems/ |access-date=20 December 2024 |website=The Race |language=en}}</ref> [[Jolyon Palmer]] notes that Russell takes particularly wide exits to generate as much speed as possible, and said that Russell's precise car control allows him to survive risky turns.<ref name=":23">{{Cite web |title=How Russell pushes the limits in high speed corners {{!}} Racing ID |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/video/how-russell-pushes-the-limits-in-high-speed-corners-racing-id.1790170576769102317 |access-date=20 December 2024 |website=Formula 1® - The Official F1® Website |language=en}}</ref> Russell's style takes advantage of high-grip tracks and high-[[downforce]] cars.<ref name=":55">{{Cite web |last=Straw |first=Edd |date=2026-06-10 |title=How Russell's driving style is feeding into 2026 struggles |url=https://www.the-race.com/formula-1/george-russell-driving-style-f1-2026-struggles-kimi-antonelli/ |access-date=2026-07-05 |website=The Race |language=en}}</ref>

Russell's racing has been described as "analytical" and "situational,"<ref>{{Cite web |last=Bishop |first=Matt |date=2026-02-24 |title=Matt Bishop: 'I'm backing Russell to beat Verstappen in bitter 2026 F1 title duel' |url=https://www.motorsportmagazine.com/articles/single-seaters/f1/matt-bishop-im-backing-russell-to-beat-verstappen-in-bitter-2026-f1-title-duel/ |access-date=2026-03-23 |website=Motor Sport Magazine |language=en-GB}}</ref> and he adapts his driving to track and car conditions.<ref name=":52" /> After Mercedes announced Russell's promotion to the senior team from Williams, Williams's Dave Robson highlighted his driver's adaptability.<ref name=":31">{{Cite news |last=Kalinauckas |first=Alex |date=16 December 2021 |title=Autosport 2021 Top 50: #12 George Russell |url=https://www.autosport.com/general/news/autosport-2021-top-50-12-george-russell/6885283/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211217092435/https://www.autosport.com/general/news/autosport-2021-top-50-12-george-russell/6885283/ |archive-date=17 December 2021 |access-date=5 March 2025 |work=[[Autosport]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |language=en |url-status=live }}</ref> In his junior and early career, Russell's smooth driving style was compared to that of [[Jenson Button]].<ref name=":19" /> However, Robson suggested that Russell sought to strike a balance between Button and Lewis Hamilton.<ref name=":31" /> Since joining Mercedes, Russell adapted his driving to take more aggressive and direct V-shaped approaches into corners, drawing comparisons to [[Mika Häkkinen]].<ref>{{Cite news |last1=Chandhok |first1=Karun |last2=Kalinauckas |first2=Alex |date=26 January 2024 |title=The driving style secrets of F1's current stars |url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/the-driving-style-secrets-of-f1s-current-stars/10568984/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240301050256/https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/the-driving-style-secrets-of-f1s-current-stars/10568984/ |archive-date=1 March 2024 |access-date=20 December 2024 |work=[[Autosport]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |language=en |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite AV media |url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7Ww0ESV3Z1A |title=The Secret To George Russell's Smooth Driving Style |date=10 August 2024 |last=((F1Unchained)) |access-date=20 December 2024 |via=YouTube}}</ref> Even so, compared to his former teammate [[Lewis Hamilton]], Russell braked earlier, turned later, and "carrie[d] more speed through the corner and exiting it."<ref name=":21">{{Cite web |last=Mitchell-Malm |first=Scott |date=16 August 2024 |title=What Hamilton hates about driving F1's current cars |url=https://www.the-race.com/formula-1/lewis-hamilton-f1-ground-effect-cars-driving-style-clash/ |access-date=20 December 2024 |website=The Race |language=en}}</ref> 

During the 2024 season, the racing press suggested that Russell's style might be a better fit for the [[Ground effect (cars)|ground effect]] cars F1 was using at the time than Hamilton's.<ref name=":21" /><ref name=":22">{{Cite web |last=Hughes |first=Mark |date=19 December 2024 |title=Revealed: Why 2024 Mercedes sapped Lewis Hamilton's pace |url=https://www.motorsportmagazine.com/archive/article/february-2025/10/revealed-why-2024-mercedes-sapped-lewis-hamiltons-pace/ |access-date=20 December 2024 |website=Motor Sport Magazine |language=en-GB}}</ref> [[Mark Hughes (journalist)|Mark Hughes]] added that Mercedes's successful midseason upgrades accentuated this F1-wide trend.<ref name=":22" /> On the other hand, ''The Race'' suggested that the 2026 regulation change hurt Russell by de-emphasizing downforce.<ref name=":55" />

=== Qualifying ===
Throughout his career, Russell has consistently been praised for his qualifying pace. At Williams, the Briton drove an unimpressive car to unexpectedly high grid placements on several occasions,<ref>{{Cite news |last=Austin |first=Dan |date=18 December 2021 |title=Formula 1 driver power rankings for 2021 after Max Verstappen beats Lewis Hamilton |url=https://www.the-independent.com/f1/f1-driver-ratings-power-ranking-2021-b1978702.html |access-date=5 March 2025 |work=The Independent}}</ref> most notably [[2021 Belgian Grand Prix|Spa 2021]] (second) and [[2021 Russian Grand Prix|Sochi 2021]] (third).<ref>{{Cite web |date=2 September 2021 |title=Latifi says 'impressive' Russell's Mr Saturday tag is misleading, as Leclerc backs Briton for Mercedes seat {{!}} Formula 1® |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/latifi-says-impressive-russells-mr-saturday-tag-is-misleading-as-leclerc.6WpGAz9hoorCwF3fhHvVnN |access-date=24 November 2024 |website=Formula 1® - The Official F1® Website}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Smith |first=Luke |date=27 September 2021 |title=10 things we learned from F1's 2021 Russian Grand Prix |url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/10-things-we-learned-from-f1s-2021-russian-grand-prix/6677198/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240919012620/https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/10-things-we-learned-from-f1s-2021-russian-grand-prix/6677198/ |archive-date=19 September 2024 |access-date=5 March 2025 |work=[[Motorsport.com]] |language=en |url-status=live }}</ref> He outqualified teammates [[Robert Kubica]] and [[Nicholas Latifi]] 57 out of 59 times.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Haldenby |first=Nicky |date=31 December 2021 |title=Nicholas Latifi's 2021 F1 season in statistics - Lights Out ●●●●● |url=https://www.lightsoutblog.com/nicholas-latifis-2021-f1-season-in-statistics/ |access-date=24 November 2024 |website=www.lightsoutblog.com}}</ref> Russell acquired the nickname "'''Mr. Saturday'''" for his Williams qualifying feats,<ref name=":30">{{Cite web |last=Clancy |first=Rebecca |date=7 September 2021 |title=George Russell: Lewis Hamilton's new team-mate is confident, popular and known as 'Mr Saturday' |url=https://www.thetimes.com/article/george-russell-is-confident-popular-and-known-as-mr-saturday-fzlt6mlpl |access-date=5 March 2025 |website=The Times |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=26 June 2021 |title=P11 'so satisfying' says Russell as Williams impress in Styria qualifying on hunt for first points {{!}} Formula 1 |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/p11-so-satisfying-says-russell-as-williams-impress-in-styria-qualifying-on.4yc85RSLWKA7D9AL6b05Zu |access-date=5 March 2025 |website=Formula 1® - The Official F1® Website |language=en}}</ref><ref name=":29" /> although he has downplayed the nickname, explaining that the goal is to win on Sunday.<ref>{{Cite web |last= |first= |date=21 March 2022 |title=Formula 1 Driver George Russell Replies to Fans on the Internet |url=https://www.gq.com/video/watch/gq-sports-actually-me-george-russell-hype-cover |access-date=24 November 2024 |website=GQ}}</ref>

At Mercedes, Russell became the only teammate in [[Lewis Hamilton]]'s career (Hamilton being Formula One's [[List of Formula One polesitters|all-time leader in pole positions]]) to outqualify him head-to-head during their time as teammates (39–29).<ref name=":15">{{Cite web |last=McDonagh |first=Connor |date=7 December 2024 |title=George Russell joins exclusive club with qualifying triumph over Lewis Hamilton |url=https://www.crash.net/f1/news/1061372/1/george-russell-joins-exclusive-club-qualifying-triumph-over-lewis-hamilton |access-date=9 December 2024 |website=www.crash.net}}</ref> Although Hamilton outqualified Russell 13–9 in their first season together, Russell reached parity in 2023 and beat Hamilton 19–5 in 2024,<ref name=":15" /> becoming one of only two teammates (the other being 2016 champion [[Nico Rosberg]]) to outqualify him in a single season.<ref>{{Cite web |date=31 December 2024 |title=F1: Final 2024 team-mate qualifying and race head-to-head scores featuring Lewis Hamilton vs George Russell and more |url=https://www.skysports.com/f1/news/12028/13274967/f1-final-2024-team-mate-qualifying-and-race-head-to-head-scores-featuring-lewis-hamilton-vs-george-russell-and-more |access-date=5 March 2025 |website=Sky Sports |language=en}}</ref>

=== Racecraft ===
According to [[Karun Chandhok]], Russell "is generally one of the cleanest racers" in F1.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Chandhok |first=Karun |date=29 April 2023 |title="I understand why Max was upset..." |url=https://x.com/karunchandhok/status/1652327537291190278 |access-date=24 November 2024 |website=Twitter}}</ref> Several drivers have noted Russell's clean racing on track, including teammate [[Lewis Hamilton]]<ref>{{Cite web |date=28 October 2024 |title='Neither of us are silly' says Hamilton after Russell battle |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/neither-of-us-are-silly-says-hamilton-as-he-bests-russell-in-mercedes-mexico.21dukBtjffXIAdbTxXkWTy |access-date=5 December 2024 |website=Formula 1® - The Official F1® Website}}</ref> and [[Sebastian Vettel]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Gale |first=Ewan |date=25 October 2021 |title=Vettel praises "fair" Russell racecraft after points return |url=https://www.gpfans.com/en/f1-news/71325/vettel-praises-fair-russell-racecraft-after-points-return/ |access-date=24 November 2024 |website=GPfans}}</ref> In addition, at the [[2022 British Grand Prix]], Russell jumped out of his car to check on [[Zhou Guanyu]] following a major first-lap crash, even though it triggered his own retirement from the race.<ref>{{Cite web |date=4 July 2022 |title='I wanted to see if I could help' – Russell on his post-Zhou crash reaction, and why he was frustrated not to take the restart |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.i-wanted-to-see-if-i-could-help-russell-on-his-brave-post-zhou-crash.1W0qQ5zoChzwYaIpcbhWG2.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220704115526/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.i-wanted-to-see-if-i-could-help-russell-on-his-brave-post-zhou-crash.1W0qQ5zoChzwYaIpcbhWG2.html |archive-date=4 July 2022 |access-date=4 July 2022 |website=Formula1}}</ref> (The crash occurred after [[Pierre Gasly]] and Russell collided at the start of the race, bumping Russell into Zhou.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Benson |first=Andrew |date=3 July 2022 |title=British Grand Prix: George Russell says Formula 1 needs to learn from Zhou Guanyu crash |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/formula1/62031509 |access-date=5 March 2025 |work=BBC Sport |language=en-GB}}</ref>) However, after Russell questioned [[Charles Leclerc]]'s defensive tactics during the [[2023 British Grand Prix]], Ferrari team principal [[Frédéric Vasseur]] noted that Russell had used similar tactics to defend his position in prior races, explaining that "that's life" in Formula One.<ref>{{Cite web |date=10 July 2023 |title=Ferrari boss hits back at George Russell over Charles Leclerc criticism |url=https://metro.co.uk/2023/07/10/f1-george-russell-called-out-after-slamming-charles-leclerc-at-british-gp-19100260/ |access-date=5 March 2025 |website=Metro |language=en}}</ref>

Russell's racecraft has received some criticism, as Russell has not always converted high grid placements into high finishes. As a rookie, Russell was plagued by poor starts; that year, "he started lap two behind [teammate Robert] Kubica 11 times despite his qualifying superiority."<ref name=":7">{{Cite web |last=Straw |first=Edd |date=7 September 2021 |title=Is Mercedes swapping one 'Mr Saturday' for another? |url=https://www.the-race.com/formula-1/is-mercedes-swapping-one-mr-saturday-for-another/ |access-date=24 November 2024 |website=The Race}}</ref> More broadly, it took Russell two and a half seasons to score his first points at Williams. ''The Race'' responded that Russell's race day struggles at Williams were primarily the fault of the car, reasoning that Russell's strong grid placements at Williams were "in a constant battle against regression to the mean," and it was "inevitable that his Sunday results [were] less impressive."<ref name=":7" /> During Russell's years at Williams, [[Fernando Alonso]] said that Russell had great natural speed and "surprises me every weekend".<ref name=":29" /> Following Russell's second-place finish at the [[2025 Bahrain Grand Prix]], [[Peter Windsor]] called Russell's drive "one of the best I've seen in a long, long time", praising his tyre management (Russell nursed a set of used soft tyres for over twenty laps), on-the-fly adjustments to various mechanical issues, and defensive positioning against third-placed [[Lando Norris]], who had the faster car and the tyre advantage at the end of the race.<ref name=":41">{{Cite AV media |url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VVrsd8_9-TY |title=2025 F1 BAHRAIN GRAND PRIX by Peter Windsor |date=13 April 2025 |last=Peter Windsor |access-date=13 April 2025 |via=YouTube}} (2:00-3:33)</ref>

Russell's tyre management has alternately been praised and criticised. He was praised for his tyre management at Williams.<ref name=":7" /> Upon joining Mercedes, he overextended his tyres on several occasions, contributing to some disappointing results.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Anderson |first=Ben |date=17 June 2024 |title=Is Russell too limited to become Mercedes' F1 team leader? |url=https://www.the-race.com/formula-1/is-george-russell-too-error-prone-to-lead-mercedes/ |access-date=24 November 2024 |website=The Race}}</ref> His tyre management received renewed praise during the 2024 season, following strong performances at [[2024 Belgian Grand Prix|Spa]],<ref>{{Cite web |last=Noble |first=Jonathan |date=29 July 2024 |title=Were Russell's Worn Tyres the Cause of His Spa F1 Disqualification? |url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/were-russells-worn-tyres-the-cause-of-his-spa-f1-disqualification/10640095/ |access-date=24 November 2024 |website=Motorsport.com}}</ref> [[2024 United States Grand Prix|Austin]],<ref>{{Cite web |last=Szabo |first=Balazs |date=21 October 2024 |title=Mercedes takes delight in encouraging tyre management after tough Austin weekend |url=https://www.f1technical.net/news/25665 |access-date=24 November 2024 |website=www.f1technical.net}}</ref> and [[2024 Monaco Grand Prix|Monaco]].<ref>{{Cite AV media |url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dQqfkALAwvQ |title=2024 F1 Monaco GP analysis by Peter Windsor |date=26 May 2024 |last=Peter Windsor |access-date=5 March 2025 |via=YouTube}} (8:30-8:33)</ref>

Although Russell prioritized consistency during his first season with Mercedes, he began taking greater risks in the following seasons, and committed several high-profile mistakes, notably during the [[2024 Canadian Grand Prix]], where ''[[Motor Sport (magazine)|Motor Sport]]'' thought he botched Mercedes's first real chance at a win since 2022.<ref name=":14">{{Cite web |last=Kisby |first=Cambridge |date=13 June 2024 |title=Does George Russell make too many mistakes? |url=https://www.motorsportmagazine.com/articles/opinions/does-george-russell-make-too-many-mistakes/ |access-date=24 November 2024 |website=Motor Sport Magazine}}</ref> Following that race, Russell admitted that he "need[s] to dial down the risk/reward [ratio] of how hard I'm driving," but explained that "I'd prefer finishing P6 every race and having two victories rather than finishing P5, P4, P3 every race and not get the race victory."<ref>{{Cite web |last=Kalinauckas |first=Alex |date=3 July 2024 |title=Russell Hits Back at 'Mistakes Under Pressure' F1 Critics |url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/russell-hits-back-at-mistakes-under-pressure-f1-critics/10630711/ |access-date=24 November 2024 |website=Motorsport.com}}</ref> He picked up two victories later that season. His {{F1|2025}} season was praised for its consistency,<ref>{{Cite news |last=Slater |first=Luke |date=7 October 2025 |title=George Russell is the best Briton in F1, not Lando Norris |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/formula-1/2025/10/07/george-russell-best-briton-f1-grid/ |access-date=7 October 2025 |work=The Telegraph |language=en-GB |issn=0307-1235}}</ref> with ''The Race'' remarking that Russell was "the only driver who made fewer significant errors than [Max] [[Max Verstappen|Verstappen]] in 2025."<ref name=":51" />

=== Records and statistical oddities ===
{{See also|List of Formula One driver records}}
[[File:Kart Silverstone 20260423 Russell Helmets (cropped2).jpg|thumb|right|Russell's helmets from {{F1|2019}} to {{F1|2025}} on display at [[Silverstone Circuit|Silverstone]]|alt=Nine of Russell's helmets displayed on a wall in a three-by-three grid]]

Russell holds the record for most pit stops in a single race (7 at the [[2023 Dutch Grand Prix]]), shared with [[Lance Stroll]], [[Liam Lawson]], and [[Alain Prost]]. Russell, Stroll, and Lawson all tied Prost's record at the same race.<ref name=":13" />

Russell and [[Max Verstappen]] are one of two sets of drivers to tie for P1 in qualifying in Formula One history, at the [[2024 Canadian Grand Prix]]. Previously, [[Jacques Villeneuve]], [[Michael Schumacher]], and [[Heinz-Harald Frentzen]] tied in qualifying at the [[1997 European Grand Prix]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=de Celis |first=Jose Carlos |date=9 June 2024 |title=The F1 Rule that Gave Pole to Russell over Verstappen After Setting the Same Time |url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/the-f1-rule-that-gave-pole-to-russell-over-verstappen-after-setting-the-same-time/10621258/ |access-date=30 November 2024 |website=Motorsport.com}}</ref> He tied with Verstappen again at the [[2025 Spanish Grand Prix]], this time for P3.<ref name=":44">{{Cite news |last=Pryson |first=Mike |date=31 May 2025 |title=F1 Spanish Grand Prix Qualifying Is Another 'Mega' Day for McLaren |url=https://www.autoweek.com/racing/formula-1/a64934886/f1-spanish-grand-prix-qualifying-another-mega-mclaren/ |access-date=1 June 2025 |work=Autoweek}}</ref>

At the [[2024 Belgian Grand Prix]], Russell became the sixth driver in Formula One history to lose a race win by disqualification.<ref name=":20">{{Cite web |last=Hardy |first=Ed |date=30 June 2024 |title=All the F1 Drivers Disqualified After Winning a Grand Prix |url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/f1-drivers-to-have-been-disqualified-after-winning-a-grand-prix/10640308/ |access-date=30 November 2024 |website=Motorsport.com}}</ref>

==Other ventures==
[[File:FIA F1 Austria 2022 George Russell (2) (cropped).jpg|thumb|left|upright|Russell at the [[2022 Austrian Grand Prix]]]]
Since 2021, Russell has served as a director of the [[Grand Prix Drivers' Association]] (GPDA), the Formula One drivers' trade union.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Noble |first=Jonathon |date=23 March 2021 |title=F1 news: Russell replaces Grosjean as GPDA director |url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/russell-new-gpda-director-grosjean/5862512/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210624204317/https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/russell-new-gpda-director-grosjean/5862512/ |archive-date=24 June 2021 |access-date=23 March 2021 |website=Motorsport.com}}</ref> His primary role at the GPDA is to relay the paddock's concerns about safety, racing quality, and the junior driver pipeline to the GPDA's full-time personnel.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Larkam |first=Lewis |date=20 April 2023 |title=George Russell explains what his F1 GPDA director role actually means {{!}} F1 {{!}} Crash |url=https://www.crash.net/f1/news/1024510/1/russell-explains-what-his-f1-gpda-director-role-actually-means |access-date=16 October 2024 |website=www.crash.net}}</ref>

The [[GB4 Championship]] awards the George Russell Pole Position Cup to the driver who takes the most pole positions in a given season.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.gb-4.net/news/2022/gb4-championship-to-award-george-russell-pole-position-cup-in-2022|title=GB4 CHAMPIONSHIP TO AWARD GEORGE RUSSELL POLE POSITION CUP IN 2022|website=gb-4.net|accessdate=21 September 2022|archive-date=21 September 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220921161656/https://www.gb-4.net/news/2022/gb4-championship-to-award-george-russell-pole-position-cup-in-2022|url-status=live}}</ref>

Like many Formula One drivers, Russell has participated in the ''[[Formula 1: Drive to Survive]]'' television show. The show's coverage of Russell has primarily focused on his efforts to join and stay at Mercedes. The [[Formula 1: Drive to Survive season 4|fourth season]] (2022) traces his efforts to obtain the second Mercedes seat for 2022, when [[Valtteri Bottas]]'s contract expired, and includes a scene in which [[Toto Wolff]] informs Russell of his promotion, which ''[[Motor Sport (magazine)|Motor Sport]]'' thought was staged for the cameras.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Elson |first=James |date=3 March 2022 |title=F1 Drive to Survive Season 4: Episode synopsis |url=https://www.motorsportmagazine.com/articles/drive-to-survive/f1-drive-to-survive-season-4-episode-synopsis/ |access-date=7 March 2025 |website=Motor Sport Magazine |language=en-GB}}</ref> The [[Formula 1: Drive to Survive season 7|seventh season]] (2025) details Russell's efforts to earn a leadership role at Mercedes after [[Lewis Hamilton]] announced his departure for Ferrari, and suggested that Russell secured his place in Mercedes by winning the [[2024 Belgian Grand Prix]], when in reality, he was disqualified from that race. Russell was also a featured narrator in the episode about the [[2024 Singapore Grand Prix]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Elson |first=James |date=7 March 2025 |title=What happens in Drive to Survive Season 7? Episode Synopsis |url=https://www.motorsportmagazine.com/articles/single-seaters/f1/what-happens-in-drive-to-survive-s7-episode-synopsis/ |access-date=7 March 2025 |website=Motor Sport Magazine |language=en-GB}}</ref> In 2024, Russell said that while he understands some "people are upset that everything is dramatized" in the show, he accepts the show's style as long as it draws new fans into the sport.<ref>{{Cite web |date=27 February 2024 |title=George Russell is Okay with Fakery of Netflix F1 Series 'Drive to Survive' |url=https://www.autoweek.com/racing/formula-1/a46996112/george-russell-okay-fakery-netflix-f1-drive-survive/ |access-date=7 March 2025 |website=Autoweek |language=en-US}}</ref>

==Personal life==
Since 2020, Russell has been in a relationship with Carmen Montero Mundt;<ref name=":30" /> the couple reside in [[Monaco]]. They were introduced to each other by mutual friends in [[London]].<ref>{{cite web |last1=England |first1=Adam |date=22 February 2024 |title=Who Is George Russell's Girlfriend? All About Carmen Montero Mundt |url=https://people.com/who-is-carmen-montero-mundt-george-russell-8400095 |access-date=19 May 2024 |website=People.com}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last1=Biswas |first1=Sabyasachi |date=13 April 2024 |title="Now We're Back Together!": GF Carmen Elated to Move in With George Russell; Prepares to Leave London |url=https://thesportsrush.com/f1-news-now-were-back-together-gf-carmen-elated-to-move-in-with-george-russell-prepares-to-leave-london/ |access-date=19 May 2024 |website=thesportsrush.com}}</ref> The couple announced their enagement on 9 August 2026.<ref>https://www.instagram.com/p/Db0xe_Djana/?utm_source=ig_web_copy_link&igsh=MzRlODBiNWFlZA==</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=George Russell makes major personal announcement |url=https://racingnews365.com/george-russell-makes-major-personal-announcement |website=Racingnews365 |access-date=9 August 2026}}</ref> He moved to Monaco in 2022.<ref name="auto" /> 

Within Formula One, Russell is friends with [[Alex Albon]],<ref>{{Cite AV media |url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=O8nBzCTdalU |title=Meet The 2025 Formula 1 Drivers! |date=10 March 2025 |last=((FORMULA 1)) |access-date=10 March 2025 |via=YouTube}} (4:18-4:21)</ref><ref>{{Cite AV media |url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qDs3mFD-t3M |title=George Russell & Alex Albon Take On The Compliment Challenge! |date=28 September 2024 |last=((FORMULA 1)) |access-date=10 March 2025 |via=YouTube}}</ref> as well as [[Lando Norris]] and [[Charles Leclerc]], with whom he and Albon streamed racing games on [[Twitch (service)|Twitch]] during the [[COVID-19 pandemic]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=23 September 2020 |title='We're there for each other' – Albon on the camaraderie of F1's 'Twitch' generation {{!}} Formula 1® |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/were-there-for-each-other-albon-on-the-camaraderie-of-f1s-twitch-generation.1IEbirL0eRz6mShqtxRJS0 |access-date=5 March 2025 |website=Formula 1® - The Official F1® Website |language=en}}</ref> Russell said that Albon helped him get into a top karting team,<ref name=":18" /> and Albon said that Russell campaigned for Williams to give him Russell's open seat after Russell left for Mercedes.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Smith |first=Luke |date=18 September 2021 |title=Albon owes Russell 'a couple of beers' for Williams F1 seat |url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/albon-owes-russell-beer-williams-seat/6668077/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230204092345/https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/albon-owes-russell-beer-williams-seat/6668077/ |archive-date=4 February 2023 |access-date=5 March 2025 |work=[[Motorsport.com]] |language=en |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=ANALYSIS: Why Williams chose Albon as Russell's replacement – and retained Latifi for 2022 {{!}} Formula 1® |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/analysis-why-williams-chose-albon-as-russells-replacement-and-retained.5mBd30IWzau4VeFiwt9C4g |access-date=5 March 2025 |website=Formula 1® - The Official F1® Website |language=en}}</ref> He is also friends with [[Fernando Alonso]], who has called him a "future world champ".<ref name=":29" /><ref>{{Cite web |last=Benson |first=Andrew |date=6 December 2024 |title=Russell v Verstappen - what's going on? |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/formula1/articles/cevg9w8440ko |access-date=5 March 2025 |website=BBC Sport |language=en-GB}}</ref>

Apart from Formula One, Russell enjoys [[padel]] and [[Freediving|free-diving]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Edmondson |first=Laurence |date=15 December 2023 |title=Russell on his 'strange' 2023 and year two alongside Hamilton |url=https://www.espn.co.uk/f1/story/_/id/39118271/george-russell-freediving-rating-strange-season-measuring-lewis-hamilton |access-date=5 August 2025 |website=ESPN.com |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{cite podcast |host=[[Spencer Matthews]] |date=4 August 2025 |title=George Russell Exclusive: Letting My Father Down & My Future at Mercedes? |url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qiEfLJa7wpM&t=1361s&ab_channel=UNTAPPED |work=UNTAPPED |publisher=High Performance |time= |access-date=5 August 2025}}</ref> He is a fan of [[Wolverhampton Wanderers]] Football Club, where his father is a season-ticket holder. He was a special guest at [[Molineux Stadium|Molineux]] in 2021.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Townley |first=John |date=7 September 2021 |title=Rising F1 star George Russell makes brilliant Wolves admission |url=https://www.birminghammail.co.uk/sport/football/football-news/rising-f1-star-george-russell-21509522 |access-date=16 October 2024 |website=Birmingham Live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Wilson |first=Andy |date=15 December 2020 |title=George Russell football team: Who does the F1 star support? |url=https://www.express.co.uk/sport/f1-autosport/1372942/George-Russell-football-team-support-Wolves-Russell-F1-evg |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220330103950/https://www.express.co.uk/sport/f1-autosport/1372942/George-Russell-football-team-support-Wolves-Russell-F1-evg |archive-date=30 March 2022 |access-date=30 March 2022 |website=Express.co.uk}}</ref>

Russell is vocal about mental health issues. He works with a psychologist and claims that it helps him perform better on track.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Davies |first1=Daniel |date=1 February 2023 |title=Formula 1 Driver George Russell Talks Therapy, Masculinity and 'Mental Maintenance' |url=https://www.menshealth.com/uk/mental-strength/a42728574/george-russell-mental-health/ |access-date=19 May 2024 |website=Men's Health}}</ref><ref name=":43" />

